// ===== CHANGELOG (last 5, per convention #26; full history in the Claude Project handoff doc) =====
// v7.82: CE10295 "main body too long" fix, round 2 (v7.80/v7.81's new top-level statements tripped it
//   again) -- 6 separate call-value vars collapsed into one float[], the two per-bar `if` blocks merged
//   into one. No library change. Import line corrected to /57 (user-confirmed real publish number).
// v7.83: comment-only trim -- this header and several long inline explanatory comments in the Auto
//   Trade Setup section shortened/removed per direct request ("can we get rid of some comments?"). Zero
//   executable code touched. CONFIRMED INSUFFICIENT -- CE10295 still reported on the v7.83 tab.
// v7.84: CE10295 fix, round 3 -- the real fix. Comments do NOT count toward the limit (v7.83 proved
//   that); the ~50-line trigger `if` block (level-pick math, handle-snap overrides) was still sitting
//   directly in the main body even nested inside an `if`. Collapsed into ONE library call,
//   obLib.f_ats_compute_trigger(). REQUIRES the library to be republished first (new export) -- import
//   line stays at /57 until you report back the real published number.
// v7.85: proactive headroom, per direct request ("move more into the libraries..."). The largest
//   remaining top-level block (CBC Flip lines/BRSG zone/HTF Flip FVG zone/HTF-LTF-MTF pivot lines --
//   21 var decls + ~105 lines) collapsed into ONE library call, obLib.f_render_flip_brsg_fvg_piv_lines().
//   ALSO requires the library republished first (another new export). See the Claude Project handoff
//   doc for full historical detail on every round above.
// v7.86: bug fix (bad drag-handle value), per direct report ("set tp1 to 1 and last image seems wrong -
//   notice the whole setup changed"; also "where is TP2"). TP2-missing was investigated and confirmed NOT
//   a bug -- f_ats_compute_trigger() correctly returns na for TP2 when there's no candidate level beyond
//   TP1 in the trade direction, and the label gate was already wired correctly end-to-end; no code change
//   needed there. The handle report WAS a real bug: no drag handle had any upper/lower sanity check, only
//   `!= 0.0`, so a stray literal price like 1 (vs. an instrument trading near 7800) was treated as fully
//   active -- it both (a) snapped TP1 to whatever the smallest real candidate in the whole pool was, with
//   no regard for which side of entry it landed on, and (b) forced the chart's autoscale to stretch down
//   to include price 1, visually crushing the entire normal price range flat (the "curved line"/"whole
//   setup changed" look). New library export f_ats_handle_sane(handle, current) gates both the handle-
//   snap override (f_ats_handle_snap) and the on-chart handle label (f_ats_draw_handles) on the handle
//   being within a plausible band of the current price (1/5th to 5x) -- an out-of-band handle is now
//   treated exactly like the inactive 0.0 default. No main-script call-site changes were needed (both
//   functions keep their existing signatures). REQUIRES the library to be republished first (same
//   f_ats_handle_snap/f_ats_draw_handles export names, changed bodies) -- import line stays at /57 until
//   you report back the real published number. See the Claude Project handoff doc for full detail.
// v7.87: pure input-reordering, per direct request ("move to top of the inputs... I can't seem to
//   select it"). The 4 drag-handle inputs (TP1/SL1/TP2/SL2) moved from the very bottom of the Auto Trade
//   Setup group to right after the main "Auto-Draw Trade Setup" enable toggle -- they used to sit past 2
//   dropdowns, 2 color-pickers, a Show TP2/SL2 pair, and 2 more dropdowns, a long scroll that made a
//   specific field easy to lose track of. Declaration order only changes the Settings panel's display
//   order within a group -- no input here reads another input's value at declaration time, so this is a
//   zero-behavior-change layout move, same tooltips (updated to mention v7.86's new out-of-range guard),
//   same downstream gating logic untouched.
// v7.88: same handles moved ONE MORE SPOT, per direct follow-up on a v7.87 screenshot ("move input to
//   the top first item when looking at settings") -- now the literal first 4 items in the group, ahead
//   of the "Auto-Draw Trade Setup" enable toggle itself. Same pure declaration-order move, zero behavior
//   change, no library change.
// v7.89: TWO changes, per direct follow-up once the v7.86 fix let the cyan handle label finally render.
//   (1) "i moved it but it did not snap" -- a drag handle used to only affect the NEXT new trigger;
//   obLib.f_ats_draw_setup() now re-applies the handle-snap check every bar against the ALREADY-drawn
//   setup, moving that level's line/label and reshaping its zone box live (per direct confirmation,
//   "Live-update the active setup") -- this is also what makes the reward/risk zone visually shade/
//   stretch as a handle moves, the second part of the same request. (2) "can we feed the values into the
//   inputs" -- not possible (Pine has no script-to-input write path, confirmed this round); closest
//   substitute is that every TP1/SL1/TP2/SL2 label AND each handle's own identifier label now show their
//   live numeric price in the text itself, so the exact value is readable straight off the chart.
//   obLib.f_ats_draw_setup() signature grew 11->17 params (added the 4 handles + a shared `tol` + the
//   candidate pool); obLib.f_ats_draw_handles()'s signature is unchanged. REQUIRES the library
//   republished first (changed bodies + f_ats_draw_setup's new params) -- import line stays at /57.
// v7.90: compile fix (CE10173), per direct report (VS Code Pine linter screenshot) -- `var bool
//   active_long = na` fails because a bare `na` literal cannot be assigned directly to a variable
//   declared with an explicit `bool` type; Pine requires an explicit type cast. Fixed to
//   `var bool active_long = bool(na)`. No other logic changed. Library bumped to session-local v66
//   (this is the only change in the library this round).
// v7.91: pure input reordering, per direct request ("move auto trade setup inputs to the top - put
//   auto setup where the blue arrow points", pointing at the "LTF Signals" group header in a settings
//   screenshot). The entire Auto Trade Setup input group (grp_trade_setup and all 17 of its inputs --
//   the 4 drag handles, the enable toggle, both triggers, both zone colors, the Stop/Target/SL2/TP2
//   level pickers, and the Show TP2/Show SL2 toggles) moved from deep in the file (right before the
//   candidate-pool builder) to the very top of the script -- now the literal first input group in the
//   whole Settings panel, ahead of even "LTF Signals" (previously the first group). Zero behavior
//   change: none of these inputs reads another input's value at declaration time, and the drawing/
//   trigger logic that consumes them (still in its original location) resolves them by name, not by
//   proximity. No library change this round.
// v7.92: new feature, per direct request ("can we have the script be able to take in +1 or -1 to
//   move target away from target(+), etc"). The 4 drag handles now accept a STEP COUNT as an
//   alternative to an absolute price: any small whole number (1 to 20, or -1 to -20) is read as "N
//   pivots further out than whatever Automatic (nearest) already picked" (+N) or "N pivots back
//   toward this level's own anchor" (-N, entry for TP1/SL1, the resolved TP1/SL1 price for TP2/SL2),
//   confirmed via AskUserQuestion as relative to today's automatic pick rather than counted from
//   entry, and coexisting with the existing absolute-price mode rather than replacing it. New library
//   exports f_ats_handle_is_step()/f_ats_handle_step(); f_ats_handle_snap() gained a 6th parameter
//   (base_ref) so it can bound how far a negative step is allowed to walk back. No on-chart handle
//   label is drawn for a step value (the existing sanity gate already excludes small integers, which
//   also protects against the v7.86 autoscale-crush bug) -- there's nothing to literally drag in step
//   mode anyway. REQUIRES the library republished first (f_ats_handle_snap()'s new signature) --
//   import line stays at /57.
//   v7.93 (09/26/2026): library renamed CBC_OrderBlocksLib -> sslib (file sslib.pine, library
//   title "sslib"). Import line changed to samuelsuss8/sslib/1 (a renamed library is a NEW library on
//   TradingView, so its first publish is version 1). No logic change. REQUIRES sslib published first.
//   v7.94 (09/26/2026): sslib v69 fix -- step-count handles (+1/-1) re-stepped every bar and ran
//   TP/SL out to the last pivot. Now applied once at trigger. Library-only change; import stays /1.
//   v7.95 (09/26/2026): library name reverted sslib -> CBC_OrderBlocksLib; import back to
//   CBC_OrderBlocksLib (number must be updated to the new published version). No logic change.
//   v7.96 (09/26/2026): import -> CBC_OrderBlocksLib/63 (user-confirmed published number). The 4
//   handle inputs renamed "TP1/SL1/TP2/SL2 step (+1 farther / -1 closer)" with step-first tooltips,
//   per user: no dragging wanted, just +1/-1 snapping. Same input variables/logic.
//   v7.97 (09/27/2026): Pivot Points table shows only the nearest N levels each side of price (new
//   input, default 8; 0 = all) -- R2/R3/YD-H were cut off past the chart edge. Library v71
//   (f_render_pivot_table +1 param). REQUIRES library republished; import stays /63 until then.
//   v7.98 (09/27/2026): Pivot Points input group moved to right after Auto Trade Setup in Settings
//   (pure declaration-order move, no logic change, no library change). Import -> /64 (user-confirmed).
//   v7.99 (09/27/2026): TP/SL steps count every level like the Pivot Points table (same-price levels
//   count separately); R2/R3/S2/S3 "table only" toggles now feed the Auto Trade Setup pool. Library
//   v72 -> import /65.
//   v8.00 (09/27/2026): small Trade Levels box (TP2/TP1/Entry/Price/SL1/SL2 + pts from price), new
//   Auto Trade Setup inputs: show / position / text size. Library v73 -> import /66.
//   v8.06 (09/28/2026): Trade Levels box shows "Long"/"Short" in the Entry row's Pivot cell (library v76).
//   Import -> /69 (library must be republished).
//   v8.05 (09/27/2026): calc_bars_count = 10000 -- only the newest 10,000 bars are calculated, so settings
//   changes recalculate faster. No library change; import stays /68.
//   v8.04 (09/27/2026): Trade Levels "Pivot" cell shows one name by priority; hover lists all (library v75).
//   Import -> /68 (library must be republished).
//   v8.03 (09/27/2026): new "ORB-H/L label text" color input (default black) for the 6 chart ORB labels;
//   session colors still drive the Market cell and active-OR lines. No library change; import stays /67.
//   v8.02 (09/27/2026): Trade Levels box gets a 4th "Pivot" column naming each level (library v74).
//   Import -> /67 (library must be republished).
//   v8.01 (09/27/2026): Pivot Points "Table text size" default Small -> Normal, per direct request.
//   No library change; import stays /66.
//   v8.07 (09/28/2026): every on-chart marker tooltip now gets a "Fired: " timestamp, not just HTF CBC
//   Flip's own (which already had one). Per direct request ("add time stamp to all alert tooltips"),
//   made while checking a plain LTF EMA20 Pierce tooltip that had no time on it at all. The old
//   HTF-Flip-only "Confirmed: " line was removed and replaced by one shared line (same time_close +
//   f_fmt_ny_time_sec() as before) appended to marker_body right alongside the existing shared
//   Confluence Score line, so A+ Setup/Zone Entry/LTF Pierce/Key Level/VWAP Bounce/Confluence all pick
//   it up too. No library change; import stays /69.
// v8.08 (09/28/2026): Auto Trade Setup now reacts to a confirmed HTF CBC flip AGAINST the currently
//   active setup, per direct report ("WHY SHORT ENTY SETUP SINCE CBC FLIIPPED LONG BEFORE THIS TIME? iF
//   CBC FLIPS THE SETUP RESETS FOR THAT DIRECTION AND ANY OLD SETUP IS CANCELLED") and the follow-up
//   answer choosing freeze-not-delete plus an auto-redraw ("#3 BUT DRAW A NEW SETUP FOR THE REVERSE
//   DIRECTION WHEN IT IS VALID"). Confirmed real gap: nothing previously re-checked an already-drawn
//   setup against the CONFIRMED HTF direction after the fact, so a stale opposite-direction setup could
//   sit on the chart indefinitely until whatever future bar happened to fire a fresh trigger on its own.
//   obLib.f_ats_draw_setup() now takes htf_dir_bull_now/htf_dir_bear_now (the same confirmed-direction
//   booleans that already gate the trigger conditions) and, on EVERY bar, freezes the active setup the
//   instant the confirmed HTF direction disagrees with it -- same extend.none/ats_frozen treatment the
//   existing TP2/SL2 breach path already applies, so the stale setup stays visible as a historical
//   record instead of vanishing. The reverse-direction redraw itself needed no new code: the existing
//   htf_flip_bull/htf_flip_bear -> ats_trigger_long/ats_short_cond -> f_ats_compute_trigger() pipeline
//   already only fires once stop/target both resolve to real values, so "when it is valid" was already
//   satisfied by validation that pipeline has always done. Library f_ats_draw_setup() signature grew
//   17->19 params (2 new trailing bools). REQUIRES the library republished first -- import stays /69
//   until you report back the real published number.
// v8.09 (09/28/2026): Library RENAMED to "ESLib" (file now ESLib.pine) per direct request ("USING NEW
//   LIBRARY WHICH IS CURRENT FILE BUT NAME CHANGED TO ESLib"). No code change in either file. A renamed
//   library publishes on TradingView as a brand-new library, so import now points at samuelsuss8/ESLib/1
//   as a placeholder -- update the version number once you report back the real published number, per
//   the standing rule (never guessed).
// v8.10 (09/28/2026): CONFIRMED -- user reports samuelsuss8/ESLib/1 is the real published number (the
//   v8.09 placeholder was correct as-is; no import change needed). Next library revision will publish as
//   /2 -- update the import to /2 only once that republish is confirmed, per the standing rule.
// v8.11 (09/28/2026): Auto re-pick of TP/SL, per direct report ("HTF PIVOT H AND L SHOULD BE INCLUDED
//   IN THE TPS AND STOP LOSSES - HERE IT IS NOT"). HTF/LTF Piv-H/L were already in the pool, but levels
//   latched at trigger, and a pivot confirmed after the trigger never reached the setup. Library v80
//   f_ats_draw_setup() now moves any Automatic level to a newer, nearer pool level (+4 args, one per
//   level: pick == "Automatic (nearest)"). REQUIRES ESLib republished first; import set to /2 (expected
