// v8.15 (09/28/2026): runtime fix for TradingView's "Heavy script" (near 20s) warning -- the chart-level
//   label overlap merge now runs on the last bar only (was every bar; its grouping loop is O(n^3)).
//   Same on-chart result. No library change.
// v8.16 (09/28/2026): automatic HTF (blank HTF Timeframe input) is now 5x the chart timeframe, per direct
//   request ("HTF TIMEFRAME IS 5X THE LTF, I.E. LTF=3 HTF=15"). Was: <=5m chart -> 15, else -> 3.
// v8.17 (09/28/2026): setups end at 17:00 ET, per direct request ("SETUPS SHOULD ALSO TERMINATE AT 17:00
//   EST USA"). New input "End setups at 17:00 ET" (default ON). The active setup freezes on the bar
//   closing at 17:00 NY, and no new setup fires on that bar. No library change.
// v8.18 (09/28/2026): needs ESLib v83 (Trade Levels box follows the CBC direction and blanks after the
//   setup ends). No main-script logic change; import -> /4 (expected next number).
// v8.19 (09/28/2026): the active Auto Trade Setup is added to every alert's status snapshot ("Setup:",
//   "Setup TP2/TP1/Entry/SL1/SL2: price | pivot | pts from price"), per direct request. Needs ESLib v84
//   (f_ats_draw_setup now returns its state); import -> /5 (expected). Uses the "Alert: new Trade Setup" toggle.
// v8.20 (09/28/2026): alerts carry the setup only while it is VALID (active, matches the confirmed HTF
//   CBC direction, price not past SL1), per direct request. No library change.
// v8.21 (09/29/2026): new input "Include 'toward' HTF flips" (default OFF). Off: every setup trigger (HTF
//   CBC Flip, LTF/HTF EMA pierces) requires the last HTF flip to be an 'away' flip (long closed above /
//   short closed below the HTF EMA20). The HTF Flip trigger used to ignore this. No library change.
// v8.22 (09/29/2026): HTF last flip ("HTF (15m) flip: SHORT 11:15 · 5 bars ago") added as the Trade Levels
//   box's last row and as a line in the Trade Setup alert, per direct request. Needs ESLib v85 (+2 params);
//   import -> /6 (expected).
// v8.23 (09/29/2026): TP3/SL3 (next pool level beyond TP2/SL2) added to the Trade Setup alert and the
//   "Setup ..." alert lines for the Alert Feed, per direct request. Chart Trade Levels box unchanged.
//   v8.24 (09/29/2026): Trade Levels box last row shortened to "HTF Flip Short 11:15 - 9". No library change.
//   v8.25 (09/29/2026): that row now shows the flip candle open-close range: "HTF Flip Short 11-11:15 - 9".
// v8.26 (09/29/2026): 5th setup trigger "HTF Pullback - Structure Confirmed" (default ON), per direct
//   request -- that moment (close INSIDE the HTF EMA9/20 zone) was never covered by the other triggers.
//   v8.27 (09/29/2026): TP4/SL4 (next pool level beyond TP3/SL3) added to alerts for the Alert Feed. Chart box unchanged.
//   v8.28 (09/29/2026): Trade Setup alert gains a "Chart: <ticker> <tf>" line so the Alert Feed can link to the chart that generated it.
// v8.29 (09/29/2026): NEW "Order Blocks (Lux-style)" group (default OFF) -- swing/break origin-candle OBs
//   with Length, Mitigation (Close/Wick/Average), Chart/HTF timeframe, Show Last, Hide Overlap, mid-line,
//   breakers, internal buy/sell activity, volume metrics; plus "Use Lux-style Order Blocks as TP/SL
//   levels" (default OFF). Fully separate from the classic Order Blocks (untouched). Needs ESLib v86
//   (new export f_ob2_manage); import -> /7 (expected).
//   v8.30 (09/29/2026): Lux-style OB default "Internal Buy/Sell Activity" -> OFF (per the user's screenshot).
//   v8.31 (09/30/2026): Trade Setup alert also carries the Status-table snapshot (a_marker_snapshot: Market, Price, CBC, EMA clouds, VWAP, EMA 200, Structure, Opening range, Fib Zone) for the Alert Feed.
//   v8.32 (09/30/2026): Order Blocks (Lux-style) > Timeframe gains "Custom 5x" (new default): charts of 5m or less build blocks from 5x the chart period (3m -> 15m), overriding the HTF Signals setting; above 5m it uses the chart. Chart / HTF choices unchanged.
//   v8.33 (09/30/2026): HTF EMA9 Pierce / HTF EMA20 Pierce get their own alert ("• HTF EMA9 Pierce - Entry: LONG"), input "Alert: HTF EMA9 / HTF EMA20 Pierce - Entry" (default ON). Setup trigger rules unchanged (still needs the favorable close).
//   v8.34 (09/30/2026): Lux-style OB Timeframe default back to "Chart" ("Custom 5x" kept as a choice). Internal Buy/Sell Activity drawn as horizontal bars like LuxAlgo (ESLib v87 -> import /8, expected).
//   v8.35 (09/30/2026): setups + High Confluence Setup must be "away": away HTF flip (High Confluence now gated too) and, with new input "Require price past both EMA clouds" (default ON), the bar closes beyond both the chart and HTF EMA9/20 clouds.
//   v8.36 (09/30/2026): Trade Setup alert also carries the "HTF Candle (.., the one that flipped)" line so the Alert Feed status table can show the HTF flip candle range.
//   v8.37 (09/30/2026): "Include 'toward' HTF flips" now defaults ON. Alerts carry "Flip side: TOWARD" while the last HTF flip was a toward flip (status block + Trade Setup alert) so the Alert Feed can outline those setups / High Confluence alerts in yellow.
//   v8.38 (09/30/2026): new input "Pierce/Touch: pullbacks only" (default ON) -- LTF EMA20 Pierce, HTF EMA9/EMA20 Pierce and EMA20 Touch (LTF/HTF) only fire when price retreats to the line (long: prior bar low above it; short: prior bar high below it). Applies to the setups they trigger too.
//   v8.39 (09/30/2026): LTF EMA20 Pierce late confirm -- up to "LTF EMA20 Pierce: late-confirm window" (default 5) candles after a pierce, the first close above the chart EMA20 + HTF EMA9 + HTF EMA20 (below for shorts) draws the setup. Trigger text "LTF EMA20 Pierce (late, N bars after)".
//   v8.40 (10/01/2026): "Setup Ended" alert -- when a setup stops being valid (SL1 hit, HTF CBC flip against, 17:00, or a new setup) it reports reason, result pts, furthest TP reached, best/worst excursion, duration, end time. The Alert Feed shows it under ENDED in the Trade Setup box.
//   v8.41 (10/01/2026): "potential flop" flips -- if the HTF flip candle's range crosses EMA 200, VWAP, PP, R1-R3 or S1-S3, the flip gets an amber "⚠ Flop? <levels>" label (input "Label potential flop flips", default ON), a line in the flip marker tooltip, and alerts carry "Flip flop: crossed <levels>".
//   v8.42 (10/01/2026): CE10117 fix (102520 > 100256 tokens) -- Lux-style OB detection, potential-flop check and the setup outcome tracker moved into ESLib v88 (f_ob2_detect, f_flop, f_ats_track). No behavior change. Import -> ESLib/7.
//   v8.43 (10/01/2026): "Minimum SL distance (pts)" (Trade Setup, default ON, 4) -- SL1/SL2 nearer than N pts to Entry are pushed out to N (pivot "Min N"); needs ESLib v89. New setups now only fire on a CLOSED candle (no mid-candle Trade Setup alerts that vanish at the close).
//   v8.44 (10/01/2026): HTF EMA9 / HTF EMA20 Pierce get the same late confirm as LTF EMA20 Pierce -- if the pierce candle does not close back on the entry side, the first close back beyond the line within "Pierce late-confirm window" (default 5) candles draws the setup (Trigger "... (late)").
//   v8.45 (10/01/2026): Trade Levels table gets TP1/SL1 and TP2/SL2 reward:risk columns (ESLib v90). Import -> ESLib/8.
//   v8.46 (10/01/2026): reward:risk columns show one decimal (ESLib v91). Import -> ESLib/9 (= v91 if v90 was published as /8).
