// v10.46 (10/29/2026): display defaults -- Pivot Points table (bottom of the chart) OFF by default ("Show Pivot Points table on chart" unticked), Trade Levels (setup) box text Small (was Normal), Status table text Small (was Normal). Input defaults only; no logic or library change.
// v10.47 (10/29/2026): "room to the first opposing level". New library ESLib3 (f_room / f_room_txt; import ESLib3/1 PLACEHOLDER -- publish ESLib3.pine first). (1) Every Trade Setup alert gets a line "Room: <level or OB> at +x pts = y x TP1 (z ATR)" -- the nearest Trade Setup pool level or active opposing Lux-style OB beyond Entry in the trade direction. (2) New filter "Skip setup if the first opposing level / OB is within x × TP1 (per symbol/timeframe)", default empty = OFF. (3) New option "TP1 just before the first opposing level when it is nearer than TP1" (min 0.5 ATR), default OFF. Defaults change nothing; logging only until the daily stats / weekly room study support a setting. Basis: 10/29 live check (MES 3m level inside half of TP1: -1.77/setup vs +0.07; MGC 3m opposing OB before TP1: -1.63 vs +0.33; both halves).
