// v10.16 (10/18/2026): "HTF CBC flip: skip the flip setup when the flip is a flop" (ats_flg, default OFF). Flop = the flip candle crossed EMA200 / VWAP with less than the flop % (⑪, default 70) of its range on the flip side; pivots ignored. Latched per flip (htf_flp), so the pullback-wait / late-away flip entries are gated too. Only the HTF CBC Flip trigger. Replay 10/12-10/16 (actual alerts): MGC blocks 8 flip setups net -1.65, MES 4 net -6.58 -- small sample, hence OFF. ESLib2 f_is_flop, import /26 PLACEHOLDER.
// v10.15 (10/18/2026): flop exception -- the HTF flip candle crossing EMA 200 / VWAP is NOT a flop when at least X % of its range is on the flip side of that line (input "...not a flop if >= % of the candle is on the flip side", default 70, 0 = old behaviour). Pivots unchanged. Needs ESLib2 f_flop_ok -> import /26 PLACEHOLDER.
// v10.14 (10/17/2026): setup ⓘ tooltip also shows "Flip volume: buy 62% · RVOL 1.40" (same as the alert). ESLib2/25, ESLib/50 PLACEHOLDER.
// v8.87 (10/05/2026): built on v8.85 (v8.86 "1 per HTF candle" dropped). Cooldown "Min candles between setups" (5) applies after ANY setup, except: an HTF CBC Flip setup, and any setup in the NEW direction once the HTF CBC has flipped against the last setup, may draw immediately. ESLib/18.
// v8.85 (10/05/2026): setup cooldown is now an input, "Min candles between setups" default 5 (was a fixed 3). HTF CBC Flip setups still ignore it. ESLib/18.
// v8.84 (10/05/2026): ORB Fail-from and ORB Flip alert bullets split back into separate up / down checks (in v8.83 a candle that triggered BOTH the up and the down outcome would have listed only one). No other change. ESLib/18.
// v8.83 (10/05/2026): a mid-candle LTF EMA20 Touch setup now STAYS once drawn (varip latch of the touch entry price + direction for the rest of that candle), even if the candle no longer qualifies at its close. Entry = the price at the touch. Token relief: A+, ORB Pass, ORB Fail-from, ORB Flip and HTF EMA9/20 Zone long/short alert pairs merged (same text); chart-label overlap registry built from arrays. ESLib/18.
// v8.82 (10/05/2026): new trigger "Trigger: LTF EMA20 Touch (draws mid-candle)" (ON): an LTF EMA20 Touch - Pullback Entry draws a setup the moment it happens inside the candle (only this trigger skips the closed-candle rule; all other gates apply). The touch alert no longer depends on the "EMA20 touch dots" display box. "EMA20 Touch: fire intra-bar" default ON. Token relief: LTF flip, HTF flip+agreement combo, agreement and HTF EMA9/20 cross long/short alert pairs merged (same text); a_st2 shared structure lines; HTF label size passed as the input string; London OR open = NY OR open - 6.5 h. ESLib/18.
// v8.81 (10/05/2026): new input "No new setups between (ET)" ON, 1600-1800 New York time: no setup from any trigger on candles that open inside the window. Alerts and already-drawn setups are not affected. ESLib/18.
// v8.80 (10/04/2026): CE10117 fix for v8.79 (100,419 tokens; input() lines do not count, so tooltip removal did nothing). Alert builder: the 28 "needs_brsg_line := true" lines replaced by one check (any bullet other than Key Level Alert), and the VWAP / EMA 200 / HTF EMA 200 / Outside HTF ORB long+short pairs merged into one branch each with the same text. Alert wording unchanged. ESLib/18.
// v8.79 (10/04/2026): new option "Pivot reclaim (R1-R3 / S1-S3) blocks setups" (ON): same rule as the VWAP reclaim, for each of R1-R3 and S1-S3 (PP not included), same bar count. Uses the existing piv_cross_up/dn arrays. CE10117 fix (first build 100,419): tooltips removed from the 37 Status Table Fields / Order inputs (self-explanatory show/hide + row-order boxes). ESLib/18.
// v8.78 (10/04/2026): new option "VWAP reclaim blocks setups" (ON, 5 bars): HTF CBC short, a chart candle closes below VWAP and later one closes back above it -> no SHORT setup from any trigger for that candle + the next 5. Mirrored for longs. Reset at each HTF flip. Computed inside f_ats_trig.  Token trims: tooltips removed from 29 colour inputs, maxval dropped on 9 inputs, s_tks replaces 15x ticker.standard(syminfo.tickerid), f_n in 4 spots. ESLib/18.
// v8.77 (10/04/2026): new Settings group "Setup Triggers" (right after Auto Trade Setup): the 6 setup triggers one per line, each followed by its own options (LTF/HTF late windows, flip pullback wait, HTF pierce extras). Inputs moved only, no logic change. ESLib/18.
// v8.76 (10/03/2026): "Require price past both EMA clouds" default OFF. ESLib/18.
// v8.75 (10/03/2026): HTF CBC Flip setups ignore the 3-candle cooldown (a setup drawn just before the flip no longer blocks it). Other triggers keep it. ESLib/18.
// v8.74 (10/03/2026): HTF EMA9/20 pierce no longer needs the close beyond the chart EMA9/20 by default -- new input ats_htf_req_ltf (OFF) restores it. HTF late window default 1 (trade-colour candle box unchanged). ESLib/18.
// v8.73 (10/03/2026): LTF EMA20 pierce late confirm now uses the same rule as the pierce itself: close back beyond the LTF EMA20 (HTF EMA9/20 only if their "...also close beyond" boxes are on, via htf_clr). It no longer always needs the close beyond both HTF EMAs. LTF late window default 1. ESLib/18.
// v8.72 (10/03/2026): CE10295 "main body too long" fix: the setup trigger section (15 statements) and the cloud-clear rule (4) are wrapped in local functions f_ats_trig() / f_clr() returning tuples. No behavior change. ESLib/18. Also: the 30 "any_confirmed := true" lines in the alert builder replaced by checking confirmed_titles != "" (token trim).
// v8.71 (10/03/2026): ORB Retest Pass tooltips rewritten: names the session OR level and price that held (OR HIGH as support for LONG, OR LOW as resistance for SHORT) and says WITH / AGAINST the HTF CBC with what that means.
// v8.70 (10/03/2026): HTF half of "price past both EMA clouds" split into two inputs, both OFF by default: ats_req_htf9 (close beyond HTF EMA9), ats_req_htf20 (close beyond HTF EMA20). With both off the rule only checks the LTF EMA9/20 (LTF EMA20 pierce: no cloud check beyond its own EMA20 close-back). Same library. Token trim: maxval removed from 12 numeric inputs (late windows, pivot N, OB/PA lengths, flip wait, confluence threshold).
// v8.69 (10/03/2026): LTF EMA20 Pierce (and its late confirm) no longer needs the close beyond the LTF EMA9 -- only the HTF half of the "price past both EMA clouds" rule applies to it (close beyond both HTF EMA9/20); its own close-back-beyond-EMA20 check stays. Other triggers keep the full rule. Trigger text adds "(closed beyond EMA9: yes/no)". Same library. Line "Width" inputs lose maxval=4 (token trim).
// v8.68 (10/03/2026): new input ats_flip_wait_on "HTF CBC Flip: require a pullback first" default OFF -> flip setups draw at the confirmed flip again; ON = the v8.52 pullback wait (ats_flip_win_in bars). Same library as v8.67.
// v8.67 (10/03/2026): new trigger Momentum break (obLib.f_ats_momo, ESLib v99 rev6): HTF CBC confirmed + close beyond the last LTF swing high/low in the trade colour, no pullback. Default ON. Status Table Order inputs lose maxval=21 (token trim).
// v8.66 (10/03/2026): LTF and HTF pierce late-confirm windows default 0 (pierce candle only). Same library as v8.65.
// v8.65 (10/03/2026): Trade Setup Filters group (all OFF by default): Choppiness Index > 61.8 (len 14), stretched from VWAP > 3.0 x ATR in the trade direction, >= 2 HTF CBC flips in the last 8 HTF candles. Trade Setup alert gains a "Filters: CHOP x | VWAP ext x ATR | HTF flips n/8" line. Needs ESLib v99 rev5 (f_ats_filters, f_ats_flt_txt) -> /15.
// v8.64 (10/02/2026): a stop pushed out to the minimum SL distance now shows where it came from -- alert "SL2: 7775 | Min 4 (VWAP) | +4 (+1.53)", chart Pivot cell "Min 4 (VWAP)" (ESLib v99 rev 4; f_ats_atr_lv returns 13 values). ESLib/15.
// v8.63 (10/02/2026): ATR pivot text now "1.5×ATR (2.9)" (multiplier x ATR value) in the Trade Levels table and alerts (ESLib v99 rev 3). ats_alt sized 9. ESLib/15.
// v8.62 (10/02/2026): separate TP switch ats_atr_tp_on (default OFF) + TP1 x 1.5 / TP2 x 3.0 ATR; obLib.f_ats_atr_lv returns the other method's [SL1, SL2, TP1, TP2]; Trade Levels + alert show both TP pairs; ATR pivot text "1.0 ATR" etc.; alert level lines built by obLib.f_ats_lv_lines. ESLib/15 (v99 revised -- if v99 was already published as /15, publish again -> /16 and change the import).
// v8.61 (10/02/2026): needs ESLib v99 (/15). Both SL methods computed per setup (obLib.f_ats_atr_sl); the checked one is active, the other shows as info rows in the Trade Levels table (price order) and as SL1/SL2 ATR (or Piv) lines in the Trade Setup alert.
// v8.60 (10/02/2026): optional SL method ats_atr_sl_on (default OFF): SL1/SL2 = entry -/+ m1/m2 x ATR(len) on the setup candle; library auto re-pick of stops disabled in that mode; min SL still applies; alert pivot text "ATR". f_n()/f_s() helpers for "#.##" number text (na -> "—"; CE10117 relief, lexical 32556). Still ESLib/14.
// v8.59 (10/02/2026): HTF pierce late window default 5; new input ats_htf_late_color (default ON): late confirm candle must be green (long) / red (short). Still ESLib/14.
// v8.58 (10/02/2026): HTF EMA9/20 Pierce late-confirm gets its own input ats_htf_late_bars (default 1); LTF EMA20 keeps ats_ltf_late_bars (5). Still ESLib/14.
import samuelsuss8/ESLib/59 as obLib // ESLib rev38 = /59 PLACEHOLDER (publish ESLib, then set the real number)
import samuelsuss8/ESLib3/1 as ob3Lib // ESLib3 v1 = /1 PLACEHOLDER (new library: publish ESLib3.pine, then set the real number)
import samuelsuss8/ESLib2/31 as ob2Lib // ESLib2 /31 PLACEHOLDER (f_ema_dist, f_htf_cline, f_cf_txt)
s_tks = ticker.standard(syminfo.tickerid)
f_n(float x) => na(x) ? "—" : str.tostring(x, "#.##")
f_s(float x) => (x >= 0 ? "+" : "") + f_n(x)
f_d(float x) => math.abs(close - x)
string s_tfm = str.tostring(timeframe.multiplier)

const string grp_or_sessions = "▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌㉒ Opening Range (Sessions) ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━"
const string grp_pivots = "▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌㉔ Pivots & Key Levels ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━"
// v4.23 token-trim: shared const strings for tooltips that were byte-for-byte identical across
// 2-3 separate input() calls each — same hoist pattern already proven safe by grp_* above (top-level
// literal read by multiple top-level input() calls, never crossing into a function scope the way the
// v4.19 obLib.f_fmt_ny_time() hoist did).
const string tt_touch_dots = "Show dots when the bar range crosses"
const string tt_piv_lines = "Persistent dashed lines at the most"
const string tt_alert_session = "Allow alerts during this custom window"
const string tt_break_alert = "Fires once when price closes on the"
// v6.75: de-const'd (were `const string`) so the LONG/SHORT direction word can be appended per call
// site below — a compile-time const cannot embed the runtime-determined direction.
string tt_orb_r_fail = "Flip — price broke one side of the Opening Range, then fully round-tripped through the opposite side before ever confirming — marked at the exact bar where that round-trip happened, not later."
string tt_orb_r_stall = "Fail from (+ or -) — price broke one side of the Opening Range but never confirmed the retest before the max-bars window expired, ending up stuck back inside the range — a stalled/timed-out breakout attempt (not a full reversal)."

enum RefLineStyle
    solid = "Solid"
    dashed = "Dashed"
    dotted = "Dotted"

f_ref_line_style(RefLineStyle s) =>
    switch s
        RefLineStyle.dashed => line.style_dashed
        RefLineStyle.dotted => line.style_dotted
        => line.style_solid

// Input
// show_background = input.bool(false, "Show Background Color")

// v7.91: the entire Auto Trade Setup input group (grp_trade_setup) moved from deep in the file to
// HERE -- the very first input group in the whole script -- per direct request ("move auto trade
// setup inputs to the top - put auto setup where the blue arrow points", pointing at the LTF Signals
// group header, i.e. "ahead of everything, including LTF Signals"). Pure declaration-order move: none
// of these inputs reads another input's value at declaration time, so this is zero behavior change,
// same as the v7.87/v7.88 in-group reorders. The library-side logic that CONSUMES these inputs (all
// the way down near the old location) is untouched -- Pine resolves top-level var/input references by
// name across the whole script, not by proximity, so moving the declarations doesn't require moving
// any of the code that uses them.
// v7.88: the 4 drag-to-snap handles moved AGAIN, this time to the literal FIRST position in the group --
// ahead of even the "Auto-Draw Trade Setup" enable toggle -- per direct follow-up ("move input to the
// top first item when looking at settings") after the v7.87 screenshot showed them second (right after
// the enable toggle, which was v7.87's own placement) rather than first. Same pure reordering as v7.87,
// zero behavior change: Pine's Settings panel displays inputs within a group in declared order, and none
// of these 4 handles (or the enable toggle) reads another input's value at declaration time.
ats_tp1_handle = input.price(0.0, "TP1 step (+1 farther / -1 closer)", confirm=false, group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="0 = Automatic (nearest level). +1 snaps TP1 one level farther from entry than the automatic pick, +2 two levels, etc. -- counted like the Pivot Points table columns, so levels at the same price each count as one step. -1 snaps it one pivot level closer to entry (never crosses entry). Whole numbers 1-20 only. If no level exists in that direction, TP1 stays where it is. Only applies while TP1's level picker is 'Automatic (nearest)'. Advanced: typing a real price instead snaps to the nearest level beyond that price.")
ats_sl1_handle = input.price(0.0, "SL1 step (+1 farther / -1 closer)", confirm=false, group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="0 = Automatic (nearest level). +1 snaps SL1 one level farther from entry than the automatic pick, +2 two levels, etc. -- counted like the Pivot Points table columns, so levels at the same price each count as one step. -1 snaps it one pivot level closer to entry (never crosses entry). Whole numbers 1-20 only. If no level exists in that direction, SL1 stays where it is. Only applies while SL1's level picker is 'Automatic (nearest)'. Advanced: typing a real price instead snaps to the nearest level beyond that price.")
ats_tp2_handle = input.price(0.0, "TP2 step (+1 farther / -1 closer)", confirm=false, group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="0 = Automatic (nearest level). +1 snaps TP2 one level farther from TP1 than the automatic pick, +2 two levels, etc. -- counted like the Pivot Points table columns, so levels at the same price each count as one step. -1 snaps it one pivot level closer to TP1 (never crosses TP1). Whole numbers 1-20 only. If no level exists in that direction, TP2 stays where it is. Only applies while TP2's level picker is 'Automatic (nearest)' and its Show toggle is on. Advanced: typing a real price instead snaps to the nearest level beyond that price.")
ats_sl2_handle = input.price(0.0, "SL2 step (+1 farther / -1 closer)", confirm=false, group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="0 = Automatic (nearest level). +1 snaps SL2 one level farther from SL1 than the automatic pick, +2 two levels, etc. -- counted like the Pivot Points table columns, so levels at the same price each count as one step. -1 snaps it one pivot level closer to SL1 (never crosses SL1). Whole numbers 1-20 only. If no level exists in that direction, SL2 stays where it is. Only applies while SL2's level picker is 'Automatic (nearest)' and its Show toggle is on. Advanced: typing a real price instead snaps to the nearest level beyond that price.")
auto_trade_setup_enabled = input.bool(true, "Auto-Draw Trade Setup (Entry/Stop/Target)", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Draws an entry/stop/target box+lines, sized from the live pivot pool below, the moment a trigger fires. Visual forecast only — Pine indicators cannot place real orders; pair this with your own execution or a webhook-driven automation if you want it to actually trade.")
// v8.77: all setup triggers in their own group, one per line, each followed by its options.
auto_trade_setup_on_ltf_pierce = input.bool(true, "Trigger: LTF EMA20 Pierce", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌② Setup Triggers ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Fires a new trade setup on every LTF EMA20 Pierce - Entry (Long/Short).")
ats_ltf_late_bars = input.int(1, "LTF pierce late-confirm window (bars)", minval=0, group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌② Setup Triggers ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v8.44: v8.58: LTF EMA20 Pierce only (HTF EMA9/20 have their own window below). If the pierce candle itself does not close back on the entry side, keep watching the next N candles: the first one that closes back beyond the line (v8.73: same rule as the pierce itself -- close back beyond the LTF EMA20; HTF EMAs only if their boxes are on), with the HTF direction unchanged and no setup drawn since the pierce, draws the setup. All other setup rules still apply. 0 = pierce candle only.")
auto_trade_setup_on_ltf_touch = input.bool(true, "Trigger: LTF EMA20 Touch (draws mid-candle)", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌② Setup Triggers ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v8.82: draws a setup on an LTF EMA20 Touch - Pullback Entry (3m CBC and HTF CBC agree, a candle moving against the trend touches the 3m EMA20, max 3 per HTF flip, 3 candles apart). Draws the moment the touch happens inside the candle -- the only trigger that does not wait for the candle close. If the candle no longer qualifies at its close, the setup disappears from the chart, but the alert has already been sent. All other setup gates (filters, VWAP / pivot reclaim, 16-18 ET window, cooldown) still apply.")
auto_trade_setup_on_htf_flip = input.bool(true, "Trigger: HTF CBC Flip (confirmed)", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌② Setup Triggers ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Fires a new trade setup on every CONFIRMED (bar-close) HTF CBC Flip. v8.75: not blocked by the 3-candle cooldown.")
ats_flip_wait_on = input.bool(false, "HTF CBC Flip: require a pullback first", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌② Setup Triggers ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v8.68: OFF (default) = the HTF CBC Flip setup draws right on the confirmed flip (all other gates still apply). ON = it waits up to the bars below for price to touch the BRSG zone or the chart EMA20 and close back in the trade direction.")
ats_flip_win_in = input.int(10, "HTF CBC Flip: wait for pullback (bars, 0 = enter at the flip)", minval=0, group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌② Setup Triggers ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v8.52: after a confirmed HTF flip the setup is NOT drawn at the flip. Step 1: within this many candles, price touches the flip's BRSG entry zone or the chart EMA20. Step 2: within this many candles of that touch, the first candle that closes back above the touched level and green (mirrored for a short) draws it. No touch or no close-back in time = no setup. 0 = old behavior (draw at the flip).")
ats_flip_two_step = input.bool(true, "HTF CBC Flip: touch and close-back may be on separate candles", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌② Setup Triggers ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v8.54 On (default): step 1 = touch of the BRSG zone / EMA20 within the window after the flip; step 2 = a green close back above it (red close below for a short) within the window after that touch. Off: the v8.52 rule -- the touch and the close-back must happen on the SAME candle, within the window after the flip.")
auto_trade_setup_on_htf_ema9 = input.bool(true, "Trigger: HTF EMA9 Pierce", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌② Setup Triggers ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Same rules as LTF EMA20 Pierce, but on the HTF EMA9 line: confirmed HTF direction + flip-away gate + this bar's range crosses the HTF EMA9 (the prior bar's didn't) + close on the favorable side. Own cooldown: once every 3 bars.")
auto_trade_setup_on_htf_ema20 = input.bool(true, "Trigger: HTF EMA20 Pierce", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌② Setup Triggers ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Same rules as LTF EMA20 Pierce, but on the HTF EMA20 line. Own cooldown: once every 3 bars.")
ats_hs_on = input.bool(false, "HTF EMA9/EMA20 Pierce replaces the current setup", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌② Setup Triggers ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v8.90: OFF (default) = HTF EMA9/20 Pierce setups wait out \"Min candles between setups\" like every other trigger. ON = an HTF EMA9 or HTF EMA20 Pierce setup ignores that wait: it draws right away and replaces the current setup (the old one ends there; kept or deleted per \"Keep previous setup when a new one fires\"). All other pierce rules still apply.")
ats_htf_late_bars = input.int(1, "HTF pierce late-confirm window (bars)", minval=0, group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌② Setup Triggers ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v8.58: HTF EMA9 / HTF EMA20 Pierce. If the pierce candle itself does not close back on the entry side, the next N candles may: the first close back beyond the line (HTF direction unchanged, no setup drawn since the pierce) draws the setup. 0 = pierce candle only.")
ats_htf_late_color = input.bool(true, "HTF pierce late confirm: trade-color candle", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌② Setup Triggers ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v8.59: during the HTF pierce late-confirm window the confirming candle must also close in the trade direction (green close > open for long, red close < open for short) as well as close back beyond the 15m EMA. Off = close beyond the line is enough.")
ats_htf_req_ltf = input.bool(false, "HTF pierce: also require close beyond LTF EMA9/20", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌② Setup Triggers ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v8.74: OFF (default) = an HTF EMA9/20 pierce only needs its close back beyond the HTF line it pierced (plus the HTF EMA boxes above if on), like the LTF EMA20 pierce. ON = the close must also be beyond the chart EMA9 and EMA20 (the old rule).")
auto_trade_setup_on_momo = input.bool(true, "Trigger: Momentum break (no pullback)", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌② Setup Triggers ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v8.67: with the HTF CBC confirmed, a closed candle that closes beyond the last confirmed LTF swing (above the swing high for a long, below the swing low for a short) in the trade colour fires a setup, no pullback needed. Each swing level fires once. All shared gates still apply (EMA clouds, filters, cooldown, closed candle).")
auto_trade_setup_on_htf_pullback = input.bool(true, "Trigger: HTF Pullback - Structure Confirmed", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌② Setup Triggers ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Draws a setup when the HTF Pullback Entry - Structure Confirmed alert fires: price just entered the HTF EMA9/20 zone, HTF structure agrees (HH/HL long, LH/LL short), recent away flip. No other trigger covers this moment, since the EMA pierces need the close OUTSIDE the zone. Needs that alert's own toggle (Alerts group) on.")
ats_allow_toward = input.bool(false, "Include 'toward' HTF flips", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="On (default since v8.37): toward-flip setups are allowed and marked \"Flip side: TOWARD\" (yellow outline in the Alert Feed). Off: setups only come after an 'away' HTF CBC flip (long flip closing ABOVE the HTF EMA20, short flip closing BELOW it). A 'toward' flip (long below / short above the HTF EMA20) draws no flip setup, and no pierce setups follow it until the next flip. On: toward flips count too, for every setup trigger. Alerts and markers are not affected.")
ats_tw_late = input.bool(true, "  ↳ toward flip: allow setups once a candle closes on the away side by (pts)", inline="ats_twl", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.55: only while 'Include toward HTF flips' is OFF. After a TOWARD HTF CBC flip, the first confirmed candle that closes at least this many points beyond the HTF EMA20 on the away side (above it for a long, below for a short; 0 = any close beyond it) counts as the flip: the HTF CBC Flip setup draws on that candle and the other triggers are allowed from then on, until the next HTF flip.")
ats_tw_pts = input.float(1.0, "", minval=0.0, step=0.25, inline="ats_twl", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_fd_mode = input.string("x ATR from 3m EMA20", "HTF CBC flip: skip setup if close is farther than", options=["Off", "pts from 3m EMA20", "x ATR from 3m EMA20", "pts from 15m EMA20", "x ATR from 15m EMA20"], inline="ats_fd", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.71/v9.78: default = x ATR from 3m EMA20, 2.0. Off = no limit. Otherwise, on the candle where the HTF CBC Flip trigger fires (incl. the late-away candle and the pullback-wait entry), the flip setup is skipped when |close - EMA20| is more than this distance, in points or in multiples of the setup ATR (ATR length above). Only the flip trigger is gated; other triggers are unchanged.")
ats_fd_x = input.float(2.0, "", minval=0.0, step=0.25, inline="ats_fd", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_fd_pts = input.string("MGC 10, MES 8, MCL 0.3, BTC 300, MNQ 50", "   ...or at least (pts) per symbol", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.89: the flip distance limit is the LARGER of the x setting above and this per-symbol point value (same symbol list format as Min SL). Unlisted symbol = x setting only. Empty = off.")
ats_fva_on = input.bool(true, "HTF CBC flip: long only if close is above VWAP and EMA200 by (pts) (mirror for short)", inline="ats_fva", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.72: OFF (default) = no check. ON = on the candle where the HTF CBC Flip trigger fires (incl. the late-away candle and the pullback-wait entry), a long needs close > VWAP + X and close > EMA200 + X; a short needs close < VWAP - X and close < EMA200 - X. Otherwise the flip setup is skipped. Only the flip trigger is gated. 0 = just beyond both.")
ats_fva_x = input.float(1.0, "", minval=0.0, step=0.25, inline="ats_fva", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_flg = input.bool(false, "HTF CBC flip: skip the flip setup when the flip is a flop (EMA200 / VWAP)", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v10.16: OFF (default) = no check. ON = no HTF CBC Flip setup (incl. pullback-wait and late-away entries) while the current HTF flip is a flop: its candle crossed EMA 200 or VWAP with less than the flop % (▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌⑪ HTF Signals, default 70) of its range on the flip side. Pivot crosses are ignored. Other triggers are not affected.")
ats_fer = input.float(0.23, "HTF CBC flip: minimum Efficiency Ratio (0 = off)", minval=0.0, maxval=1.0, step=0.01, group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.95: 0 (default) = off. Above 0 = an HTF CBC Flip setup needs the Efficiency Ratio (Trade Setup Filters chop length) on the flip candle to be at least this value, e.g. 0.30. Other triggers are not affected; the general ER filter in ③ still applies to all setups.")
ats_erl = input.float(0.08, "Minimum ER: LTF EMA20 Pierce", minval=0.0, maxval=1.0, step=0.01, inline="ats_erm", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.96: per-trigger minimum Efficiency Ratio on the trigger candle (same ER as the ③ filter). 0 (default) = off. LTF EMA20 Pierce (incl. late) / HTF EMA9 Pierce / HTF EMA20 Pierce (incl. late). Not lifted by the ③ breakout exception.")
ats_er9 = input.float(0.15, "HTF EMA9", minval=0.0, maxval=1.0, step=0.01, inline="ats_erm", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_er20 = input.float(0.15, "HTF EMA20", minval=0.0, maxval=1.0, step=0.01, inline="ats_erm", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_e2s = input.bool(false, "HTF CBC flip: EMA200 slope must agree (rising for long / falling for short)", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.90: OFF = no check. ON = an HTF CBC Flip setup needs the EMA200 now vs one HTF candle ago (e.g. 5 x 3m) to slope in the trade direction.")
ats_vws = input.bool(true, "HTF CBC flip: VWAP slope must agree (rising for long / falling for short)", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.90: OFF = no check. ON = same as above for VWAP (resets at the session start, so the first HTF candle compares against the new VWAP).")
ats_mtg = input.bool(false, "Skip setups against the MTF (60m) CBC direction", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v10.01: OFF (default) = no check. ON = no LONG setup while the last closed MTF candle's CBC is Bearish, no SHORT while it is Bullish (any trigger). Needs MTF Signals enabled (▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌⑫). The MTF CBC is always shown in the setup alert and the ⓘ tooltip.")
ats_mtg_sym = input.string("MES 2m 1", "   ...per symbol/timeframe (1 = skip, 0 = allow)", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v10.32: overrides the box above for the listed symbol / chart timeframe, e.g. \"MES 2m 1, MES 3m 0\". 1 = skip setups against the MTF (60m) CBC on that chart, 0 = allow them; unlisted charts follow the box above. Needs MTF Signals enabled (▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌⑫). 10/20 data: MES 2m against-MTF setups 16, net -21.9, worse in both halves.")
[ats_mtg_m, mtg_v] = ob2Lib.f_sym_f(ats_mtg, 1.0, ats_mtg_sym)
ats_h20s_on = input.string("Off", "Skip setups when HTF EMA slope is against the trade / min slope (pts)", options=["Off", "HTF EMA9", "HTF EMA20", "Both EMA9 + EMA20"], inline="ats_hsl", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.73/v9.75/v9.76: Off (default) = no check. Slope = the live HTF (15m) EMA now minus its value one HTF candle ago, in points. Long needs slope >= min, short needs slope <= -min (min 0 = flat or better is OK; e.g. 0.5 = must have risen/fallen at least 0.5 pts over the last HTF candle). Both = EMA9 AND EMA20 must each pass. Applies to every trigger.")
ats_hsl_min = input.float(0.0, "", minval=0.0, step=0.25, inline="ats_hsl", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_vw_blk_on = input.bool(true, "VWAP reclaim blocks setups for (bars)", inline="ats_vwb", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v8.78: HTF CBC short: once a candle closes below VWAP and a later candle closes back above it, no SHORT setup (any trigger) on that candle and the next N candles. Long mirrored (close above VWAP, then back below blocks LONG setups). Resets at each confirmed HTF flip.")
ats_vw_blk_n = input.int(5, "", minval=1, inline="ats_vwb", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_pv_blk_on = input.bool(true, "Pivot reclaim (R1-R3 / S1-S3) blocks setups (same bars)", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v8.79: same rule as the VWAP reclaim, for each of R1, R2, R3, S1, S2, S3 (not PP). HTF CBC short: a candle closes down through one of them and a later candle closes back above it -> no SHORT setup on that candle and the next N (the VWAP bars box). Long mirrored. Resets at each confirmed HTF flip.")
ats_req_clear = input.bool(false, "Require price past both EMA clouds", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v8.35: setups (every trigger) and High Confluence Setup only fire when the bar closes beyond BOTH EMA9/20 clouds: above the chart and HTF clouds for a long, below both for a short. Note: HTF Pullback triggers fire INSIDE the HTF cloud, so with this on they will almost never draw a setup; HTF EMA20 Pierce rarely will.")
ats_req_htf9 = input.bool(false, "...also close beyond the HTF EMA9", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v8.70: part of \"Require price past both EMA clouds\". ON = a long also needs the close above the HTF EMA9 (short: below). OFF (default) = the HTF EMA9 is ignored.")
ats_req_htf20 = input.bool(false, "...also close beyond the HTF EMA20", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v8.70: same for the HTF EMA20. OFF (default) = ignored.")
ats_alert_on = input.bool(true, "Alert: new Trade Setup", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Fires an alert() each time a new setup draws: direction, trigger, TP2/TP1/Entry/SL1/SL2 with pivot names and points from entry. The Alert Feed page (index v27+) shows the latest one in a box at top left. Needs an alert on this indicator set to 'Any alert() function call'.")
col_trade_setup_reward = input.color(color.new(#22C55E, 82), "Reward zone", inline="ats_col", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
col_trade_setup_risk = input.color(color.new(#EF4444, 82), "Risk zone", inline="ats_col", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_stop_level_pick = input.string("Automatic (nearest)", "Stop level", options=["Automatic (nearest)", "R3", "R2", "R1", "PP", "S1", "S2", "S3", "YD-H", "YD-L", "PMH", "PML", "HTF Piv-H", "HTF Piv-L", "HTF EQH", "HTF EQL", "LTF Piv-H", "LTF Piv-L", "EMA 200", "VWAP"], group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Pick a specific Pivot Points table level to use as the Stop instead of the automatic 'nearest pivot' logic. Applies to both triggers above. If the picked level isn't available on a given bar (e.g. HTF EQH hasn't formed yet), falls back to Automatic for that bar only.")
ats_target_level_pick = input.string("Automatic (nearest)", "Target level", options=["Automatic (nearest)", "R3", "R2", "R1", "PP", "S1", "S2", "S3", "YD-H", "YD-L", "PMH", "PML", "HTF Piv-H", "HTF Piv-L", "HTF EQH", "HTF EQL", "LTF Piv-H", "LTF Piv-L", "EMA 200", "VWAP"], group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Pick a specific Pivot Points table level to use as the Target instead of the automatic 'nearest pivot' logic. Applies to both triggers above. If the picked level isn't available on a given bar, falls back to Automatic for that bar only.")
// TP2/SL2 (v7.74): next-nearest qualifying candidate past TP1/SL1, or its own manual picker. Show
// TP2/Show SL2 (v7.76) are independent toggles (na for whichever is off is all f_ats_draw_setup() needs).
auto_trade_setup_show_tp2 = input.bool(false, "Show TP2", inline="ats_show2", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Shows the second target zone (TP1→TP2). Independent of Show SL2.")
auto_trade_setup_show_sl2 = input.bool(false, "Show SL2", inline="ats_show2", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Shows the second stop zone (SL1→SL2). Independent of Show TP2.")
col_trade_setup_reward2 = input.color(color.new(#22C55E, 90), "Reward zone 2 (TP1→TP2)", inline="ats_col2", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
col_trade_setup_risk2 = input.color(color.new(#EF4444, 90), "Risk zone 2 (SL1→SL2)", inline="ats_col2", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_stop2_level_pick = input.string("Automatic (nearest)", "SL2 level", options=["Automatic (nearest)", "R3", "R2", "R1", "PP", "S1", "S2", "S3", "YD-H", "YD-L", "PMH", "PML", "HTF Piv-H", "HTF Piv-L", "HTF EQH", "HTF EQL", "LTF Piv-H", "LTF Piv-L", "EMA 200", "VWAP"], group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Pick a specific Pivot Points table level to use as SL2 instead of the automatic next-nearest logic. Only used when 'Show SL2' is on. Falls back to Automatic for that bar if the picked level isn't available.")
ats_target2_level_pick = input.string("Automatic (nearest)", "TP2 level", options=["Automatic (nearest)", "R3", "R2", "R1", "PP", "S1", "S2", "S3", "YD-H", "YD-L", "PMH", "PML", "HTF Piv-H", "HTF Piv-L", "HTF EQH", "HTF EQL", "LTF Piv-H", "LTF Piv-L", "EMA 200", "VWAP"], group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Pick a specific Pivot Points table level to use as TP2 instead of the automatic next-nearest logic. Only used when 'Show TP2' is on. Falls back to Automatic for that bar if the picked level isn't available.")
ats_keep_old = input.bool(true, "Keep previous setup when a new one fires", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="On (default): when a new setup draws, the previous one stops extending at that bar and stays on the chart. Off: a previous setup is kept only if price touched its TP1/SL1/TP2/SL2; an untouched one is replaced.")
ats_one_on = input.bool(true, "Skip a new setup while the last same-direction setup is still running", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.61: ON (default) = while the latest setup is still live (not ended by SL1 / trail, TP2, HTF flip, 17:00 or replacement), a new setup in the SAME direction is not drawn (no box, no Trade Setup alert). An opposite-direction setup still draws. OFF = every trigger draws its own setup.")
ats_kn_on = input.bool(true, "Erase older setups, keep this many back", inline="ats_kn", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.31: ON = setups still auto-draw, but when a new one draws only it and this many earlier setups stay on the chart (rolling); every older setup (boxes, lines, labels, trail steps, ⓘ) is erased. 0 = only the newest setup. v9.33: ON, 5 back by default. OFF = earlier setups stay per the option above.")
ats_kn = input.int(50, "", minval=0, maxval=500, inline="ats_kn", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_use_ob2 = input.bool(false, "Use Lux-style Order Blocks as TP/SL levels", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Adds each active Lux-style order block's top, bottom and mid-line (OB+ H/L/M bullish, OB- H/L/M bearish) to the candidate levels the setups pick TP/SL from. Needs Order Blocks (Lux-style) > Show on.")
ats_min_sl_on = input.bool(true, "Minimum SL distance (pts) per symbol", inline="ats_msl", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.53: per symbol. If SL1 (or SL2) is nearer to Entry than the listed points for this chart's symbol, it is pushed out to exactly that distance (pivot column shows 'Min N'). A stop already farther away is unchanged. Format: SYMBOL points, comma separated (MGC 6, MES 6 ...). Full-size contracts use the micro's value (GC = MGC, ES = MES, NQ = MNQ, RTY = M2K, CL = MCL); BTC = MBT or any BTC symbol. Not listed or 0 = no minimum. Wins over the Max ATR SL1 cap if larger.")
ats_min_sl = input.string("MGC 5, MES 5, MNQ 25, M2K 3, MCL 0.3, BTC 300", "", inline="ats_msl", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
float ats_msl0 = nz(obLib.f_sl_cap(ats_min_sl_on, ats_min_sl))
ats_msl_sym = input.string("", "   ...minimum SL per symbol/timeframe (overrides; 0 = no minimum)", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v10.28: overrides the line above for a symbol and/or chart timeframe, e.g. \"MGC 3m 0, MES 3m 0\" = no fixed minimum on the 3m charts (the SL is then just SL1 x ATR). A listed value > 0 replaces the minimum; 0 removes it; unlisted charts keep the per-symbol minimum above. Replay 10/12-10/19: the 5-pt floor made the MGC 3m stop ~2.3 ATR while 90 % of winners never went more than ~1.1 ATR against.")
[msl_o, msl_v] = ob2Lib.f_sym_f(true, ats_msl0, ats_msl_sym)
ats_msl = msl_o ? msl_v : 0.0
ats_atr_sl_on = input.bool(true, "SL method: 3m ATR (instead of pivots)", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v8.60: OFF = current method (SL1/SL2 = nearest pool levels beyond entry). ON = SL1 = Entry -/+ SL1 x ATR, SL2 = Entry -/+ SL2 x ATR, using the chart-timeframe ATR on the setup candle. v8.61: the other method's SL1/SL2 are always shown too (Trade Levels table, darker red, in price order; alert lines SL1/SL2 ATR or SL1/SL2 Piv) for comparison. Stops stay fixed (no auto re-pick to pool levels; dragging a handle still works). Minimum SL distance still applies. TPs unchanged.")
ats_slm = input.string("ATR / pivots (above)", "SL1 placement", options=["ATR / pivots (above)", "15m CBC flip level", "Last 15m close"], group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v10.01: where SL1 goes. ATR / pivots = the SL method above (default). 15m CBC flip level = the low (long) / high (short) of the last CLOSED HTF (15m) candle, i.e. where 15m CBC would flip against the trade. Last 15m close = the close of the last CLOSED HTF (15m) candle. Both: clamped to the Max ATR SL1 cap and the Minimum SL distance per symbol; if the level is on the wrong side of Entry (or missing) SL1 falls back to ATR / pivots. SL2 is pushed out to at least SL1. Trade Levels / alert show the distance as x ATR. Works best with SL method 3m ATR ON (with pivots the auto re-pick can pull SL1 to a nearer pool level).")
ats_atr_len = input.int(14, "ATR length / SL1 x / SL2 x", inline="ats_atr", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_atr_m1 = input.float(1.7, "", inline="ats_atr", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_atr_m2 = input.float(3.0, "", inline="ats_atr", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_slx_sym = input.string("", "   ...SL1 x ATR per symbol/timeframe (overrides)", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v10.28: SL1 = Entry -/+ this many x ATR for the listed symbol / chart timeframe, e.g. \"MGC 3m 1.3, MES 3m 1.3\"; unlisted charts use SL1 x above (1.7). Replay 10/12-10/19: 1.2-1.3 ATR beat 1.7 + 5-pt minimum on MGC 3m and MES 3m in both halves of the data; 2m not better (keep 1.7).")
[slx_o, ats_sl_m] = ob2Lib.f_sym_f(true, ats_atr_m1, ats_slx_sym)
ats_ts_sym = input.string("", "Time stop: candles per symbol/timeframe (0 = off)", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v10.28: before TP1, the setup ends at the close of the candle where this many candles have passed and the best move in the trade direction is still below x ATR (next box). E.g. \"MGC 3m 10\". Unlisted charts: off. Ends as \"Ended: Time stop\" (exit marker TS). Replay: MGC 3m +8 pts with SL 1.3 ATR; no effect on MES 3m.")
ats_ts_x = input.float(0.5, "   ↳ time stop: minimum progress (x ATR)", minval=0.0, step=0.1, group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
[ts_on, ts_nf] = ob2Lib.f_sym_f(false, 0.0, ats_ts_sym)
ats_atr_tp_on = input.bool(true, "TP method: 3m ATR (instead of pivots)", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v8.62: separate from the SL switch. OFF = TP1/TP2 = nearest pool levels beyond entry. ON = TP1 = Entry +/- TP1 x ATR, TP2 = Entry +/- TP2 x ATR (same ATR length as the SL method). Targets stay fixed (no auto re-pick). The other method's TP1/TP2 are always shown too (Trade Levels table, darker green, in price order; alert lines TP1/TP2 ATR or TP1/TP2 Piv).")
ats_atr_t1 = input.float(1.7, "TP1 x / TP2 x", inline="ats_atr_tp", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_atr_t2 = input.float(3.0, "", inline="ats_atr_tp", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_f_chop_on = input.bool(false, "Block in chop: Choppiness Index above", inline="f1", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v8.65: Choppiness Index (chart timeframe) = 100 x log10(sum of true ranges / (highest high - lowest low)) / log10(length). Above ~61.8 = sideways / range-bound, below ~38.2 = trending. No new setup while it is above the threshold.")
ats_f_chop_max = input.float(61.8, "", inline="f1", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_f_chop_len = input.int(12, "Chop filters length (bars)", minval=2, group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.35: lookback N for the Choppiness Index and the chop filters below (ADX, Efficiency Ratio, crosses, slope, range).")
ats_c_adx_on = input.bool(false, "Block in chop: ADX below", inline="f6", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.35: ADX (length N) below the value = no trend strength -> no new setup. ~20 is the classic line.")
ats_c_adx = input.float(20.0, "", minval=1, step=1, inline="f6", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_c_er_on = input.bool(true, "Block in chop: Efficiency Ratio below", inline="f7", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.35: Kaufman Efficiency Ratio = |close - close N bars ago| / sum of every bar's |close change| over N. 1 = straight line, near 0 = back and forth. Below ~0.3 = chop.")
ats_c_er = input.float(0.23, "", minval=0.01, maxval=1, step=0.05, inline="f7", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_er_bo = input.bool(true, "  ↳ except a breakout: close through the last swing high/low or an opening-range high/low within (bars)", inline="f7b", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.94: the Efficiency Ratio block is lifted on the candle that closes through the last LTF swing high / low or any session opening-range high / low (NY / London / Asia), and for the next bars up to this count (1 = that candle only). Other filters still apply.")
ats_er_bn = input.int(3, "", minval=1, inline="f7b", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_er_bs = input.bool(false, "    ↳ skip the breakout candle itself (only the next candles)", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v10.11: OFF (default) = the ER block is lifted on the breakout candle and the following candles up to the bars above (3 = breakout candle + 2 after). ON = the breakout candle itself stays blocked; only the candles after it, up to bars - 1 (3 = the 2 candles after), are let through. 1 + ON = never. Replay 10/12-10/16: low-ER signals ON the breakout candle mostly lost, the 1-2 candles after were positive (small sample).")
ats_er_bg = input.bool(false, "  ↳ colour candles by Efficiency Ratio band (ER 0.23 and below)", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.98: background colour by ER (length = Chop filters length): dark red = 0 to 0.05, red = over 0.05 to 0.10, orange = over 0.10 to 0.15, yellow = over 0.15 to 0.20, green = over 0.20 to 0.23, no shade = above 0.23. Exact ER of any candle: hover it and read 'ER' in this indicator's status line (top-left) or the Data Window. Independent of the ER chop filter value.")
ats_c_x_on = input.bool(false, "Block in chop: EMA20 / VWAP crosses >=", inline="f8", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.35: candles in the last N whose close crossed the chart EMA20 or VWAP (vs the previous close). At or above the value = price whipping around the lines.")
ats_c_x = input.int(4, "", minval=1, inline="f8", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_c_sl_on = input.bool(false, "Block in chop: HTF EMA20 slope below (x ATR)", inline="f9", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.35: |HTF EMA20 now - N chart bars ago| / ATR below the value = the 15m trend line is flat.")
ats_c_sl = input.float(0.3, "", minval=0.01, step=0.05, inline="f9", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_c_rg_on = input.bool(false, "Block in chop: N-bar range below (x ATR)", inline="f10", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.35: (highest high - lowest low of the last N bars) / ATR below the value = tight box / squeeze.")
ats_c_rg = input.float(2.0, "", minval=0.1, step=0.1, inline="f10", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_c_st_on = input.bool(false, "Block in chop: mixed chart structure (LH + HL or HH + LL)", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.35: the latest chart-timeframe swings disagree -- Lower High with Higher Low (contracting) or Higher High with Lower Low (expanding) -- no clean trend.")
ats_f_ext_on = input.bool(false, "Block when stretched from VWAP: more than (x ATR)", inline="f2", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v8.65: no long when close is more than N x ATR above VWAP, no short when more than N x ATR below it (late, stretched entries). ATR = the Trade Setup ATR length on the chart timeframe.")
ats_f_ext_max = input.float(3.0, "", minval=0.1, step=0.1, inline="f2", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_f_ext_sym = input.string("MGC 3m 4", "   ...stretch x ATR per symbol (overrides; 0 = off)", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v10.19: per-symbol version of the line above, e.g. \"MGC 4, MES 8\". A listed symbol uses its own value and is ON even with the checkbox off; a listed 0 turns it OFF for that symbol; symbols not listed use the checkbox and number above. Replay 10/12-10/19: MGC best at 4 ATR, MES only neutral from 7-8 ATR (tighter blocked winners). v10.23: per chart timeframe too, e.g. \"MGC 3m 4, MGC 2m 0, MES 8\" -- an entry with this chart's timeframe beats a symbol-only entry (2m and 3m can differ).")
[ext_on, ext_x] = ob2Lib.f_sym_f(ats_f_ext_on, ats_f_ext_max, ats_f_ext_sym)
ats_rp_on = input.bool(false, "Skip when in the top / bottom % of a tight N-bar range", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v10.20: OFF (default) = no check. ON = no LONG while the close is in the top X % of the last N bars' high-low range AND that range is narrower than Y x ATR (no SHORT in the bottom X %). Buying the top of a tight range = chop; wide ranges (breakouts) are not affected. Replay 10/12-10/19: 24 bars / 20 % / 5 ATR blocked 27 of 86 setups (26 % win), +80.8 pts.")
ats_rp_n = input.int(24, "  ↳ N bars / zone % / range under (x ATR)", minval=5, inline="ats_rp", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_rp_z = input.float(20.0, "", minval=1, maxval=50, step=5, inline="ats_rp", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_rp_x = input.float(5.0, "", minval=0.5, step=0.5, inline="ats_rp", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_rp_sym = input.string("MGC 3m 5, MES 3m 5", "   ...range under x ATR per symbol (overrides; 0 = off)", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v10.20: e.g. \"MGC 5, MES 5\". A listed symbol is ON at its own ATR value even with the checkbox off; 0 = OFF for that symbol; others use the checkbox and Y above. v10.23: per chart timeframe too, e.g. \"MGC 3m 4, MGC 2m 0, MES 8\" -- an entry with this chart's timeframe beats a symbol-only entry (2m and 3m can differ).")
ats_rm_sym = input.string("", "Skip setup if the first opposing level / OB is within x × TP1 (per symbol/timeframe)", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v10.47: e.g. \"MES 3m 0.5, MGC 3m 1\". Empty / unlisted / 0 = off (default). Opposing level = the nearest Trade Setup pool level (pivots, YD H/L, PMH/PML, HTF/LTF pivots, EQH/EQL, EMA200, VWAP, ORs) or active Lux-style OB (⑨ Show ON; OB- for a long, OB+ for a short) beyond the close in the trade direction. TP1 = the ATR TP1 distance (after the Max TP1 cap). Every Trade Setup alert logs it as \"Room: ... = x × TP1\". 10/29 live check: MES 3m setups with a level inside half the TP1 distance -1.77/setup vs +0.07 without; MGC 3m with an opposing OB before TP1 -1.63 vs +0.33.")
ats_rm_tp = input.bool(false, "TP1 just before the first opposing level when it is nearer than TP1", inline="ats_rmtp", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v10.47: OFF (default). ON = at the setup, if the first opposing level / OB (see the line above) is nearer than TP1, TP1 is moved to 1 tick before it -- but only when that still leaves at least this many x ATR. TP2 unchanged.")
ats_rm_min = input.float(0.5, "min x ATR", minval=0.0, step=0.1, inline="ats_rmtp", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
[rp_on, rp_x] = ob2Lib.f_sym_f(ats_rp_on, ats_rp_x, ats_rp_sym)
ats_f_flip_on = input.bool(false, "Block after frequent HTF flips: flips >=", inline="f3", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v8.65: no new setup when the HTF CBC flipped at least N times within the last M HTF candles (the HTF is whipsawing inside a range).")
ats_f_flip_n = input.int(2, "", minval=1, inline="f3", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_f_flip_sym = input.string("MES 2m 4", "   ...flips >= per symbol (overrides; 0 = off)", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v10.12: per-symbol version of the line above, e.g. \"MGC 4, MES 0\". A listed symbol uses its own count (> 0 = block ON at that count, 0 = OFF), whatever the checkbox says; an unlisted symbol uses the checkbox and count above. Full-size contracts use the micro's entry (GC = MGC, ES = MES ...). Replay 10/12-10/16 (61 setups): 4+ flips cost MGC -23 pts, MES +1. v10.23: per chart timeframe too, e.g. \"MGC 3m 4, MGC 2m 0, MES 8\" -- an entry with this chart's timeframe beats a symbol-only entry (2m and 3m can differ). v10.42: default \"MES 2m 4\" (MES 2m 10/19-10/26: flips >= 4 = -34.7 pts over 9 setups, both halves negative).")
[flp_on, flp_n] = ob2Lib.f_sym_n(ats_f_flip_on, ats_f_flip_n, ats_f_flip_sym)
ats_f_flip_win = input.int(8, "in last HTF candles", minval=1, inline="f3", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_nv_on = input.bool(false, "Block if VWAP from -pts / +pts", inline="f4", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.00: HTF CBC LONG -> no new setup while the close is from 3 pts BELOW to 2 pts ABOVE VWAP (defaults). SHORT mirrored: 3 pts above to 2 pts below.")
ats_nv = input.float(3.0, "", minval=0.0, step=0.25, inline="f4", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_nv2 = input.float(2.0, "", minval=0.0, step=0.25, inline="f4", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_nv_w = input.float(1.0, "  ↳ unless the whole candle is beyond VWAP by (pts)", minval=0.0, step=0.25, group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.48: exception to the VWAP block above. LONG: if the candle's LOW (bottom wick) is at least this many points ABOVE VWAP, the setup is allowed. SHORT mirrored: HIGH at least this many points BELOW VWAP. 0 = the whole candle only has to be on the trade side of VWAP.")
ats_ne_on = input.bool(false, "Block if EMA200 from -pts / +pts", inline="f5", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.00: HTF CBC LONG -> no new setup while the close is from 3 pts BELOW to 2 pts ABOVE the chart EMA200 (defaults). SHORT mirrored: 3 pts above to 2 pts below.")
ats_ne = input.float(3.0, "", minval=0.0, step=0.25, inline="f5", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_ne2 = input.float(2.0, "", minval=0.0, step=0.25, inline="f5", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_vc_on = input.bool(false, "Skip if the Max ATR SL1 cap is below x ATR", inline="fvc", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.91: OFF = no check. ON = no new setup while the per-symbol Max ATR SL1 cap (Auto Trade Setup, e.g. MGC 7) is smaller than x times the current ATR: the stop the cap allows is too tight for the market (e.g. ATR 6.1 -> 1.5 x = 9.2 > 7 -> skip). Only when SL method = 3m ATR and the cap is ON.")
ats_vc_x = input.float(1.5, "", minval=0.0, step=0.1, inline="fvc", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_va_on = input.bool(false, "Skip while ATR is above x times ATR(100)", inline="fva", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.91: OFF = no check. ON = no new setup while the current ATR (Auto Trade Setup ATR length) is more than x times the 100-bar ATR (news / open spikes).")
ats_va_x = input.float(1.8, "", minval=0.0, step=0.1, inline="fva", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌③ Trade Setup Filters ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_trail_on = input.bool(true, "Trail SL1 after TP1 hit: x ATR", inline="ats_trl", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.07: once price reaches TP1, SL1 follows the close at this many x the 3m ATR (same ATR length as the SL method) and never moves back. Chart SL1 line/label shows \"SL1 trail\", Trade Levels Pivot cell \"Trail\"; the Setup Ended alert says \"Trail SL hit\". Off = SL1 stays fixed (as before).")
ats_trail_m = input.float(1.7, "", minval=0.1, step=0.1, inline="ats_trl", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_trail_hl = input.bool(false, "  ↳ trail from the high / low (moves live)", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.16: OFF (default) = SL1 is recalculated at each candle close: close -/+ trail x ATR. ON = it follows the highest high (long) / lowest low (short) since TP1 minus / plus trail x ATR, moving live inside the candle as price makes new highs / lows. Either way it never moves back.")
ats_part_pct = input.float(80, "Close at TP1 (%)", minval=0, maxval=100, step=5, group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.26: share of the position booked at TP1 (0 = off). The rest runs on (trailing / breakeven / flip / 17:00). Setup Ended then shows a blended result, e.g. Result: +5.2 = 0.5×6.1(TP1) + 0.5×4.3(Trail). A \"50% @ TP1\" marker is drawn on the TP1 candle.")
ats_be_on = input.bool(true, "Move remainder to breakeven at TP1", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.26: when TP1 is reached, SL1 moves to Entry (or better, if the trail is already higher), so the rest of the position cannot lose. Works with or without the trail.")
ats_tp1_sym = input.string("", "TP1 x ATR per symbol/timeframe (overrides)", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v10.31: TP1 = Entry +/- this many x ATR for the listed symbol / chart timeframe (TP method ATR), e.g. \"MGC 3m 2, MES 3m 2\"; unlisted charts use TP1 x (1.7). The per-symbol Max ATR TP1 cap still applies. Replay 10/12-10/19: 2.0 ATR beat 1.7 on MGC 3m and MES 3m.")
ats_part_sym = input.string("", "   ...close at TP1 (%) per symbol/timeframe", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v10.31: overrides \"Close at TP1 (%)\" for the listed symbol / timeframe, e.g. \"MGC 3m 50, MES 3m 80\". MGC 3m runners kept going after TP1 (50 % best); MES 3m did best with 80-100 %.")
ats_be_sym = input.string("", "   ...breakeven at TP1 per symbol/timeframe (1 = on, 0 = off)", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v10.31: overrides \"Move remainder to breakeven at TP1\" for the listed symbol / timeframe. 0 = no jump to Entry at TP1 (the trail after TP1 protects the rest). Replay: breakeven at TP1 was never better on 3m.")
[tp1_o, ats_tp_m1] = ob2Lib.f_sym_f(true, ats_atr_t1, ats_tp1_sym)
[part_o, ats_part_m] = ob2Lib.f_sym_f(true, ats_part_pct, ats_part_sym)
[ats_be_m, be_v] = ob2Lib.f_sym_f(ats_be_on, 1.0, ats_be_sym)
ats_part_alert = input.bool(true, "Alert: TP1 partial", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.26: alert on the candle that reaches TP1: close X% @ TP1, remainder %, where SL1 now is. Uses the same alert as the Trade Setup / Setup Ended alerts.")
ats_sl_lbl = input.bool(true, "Show exit markers (SL / trail / TP2 / HTF flip / 17:00 / replaced)", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.65/v9.84/v9.85: a marker on the candle every setup ends, with points on the runner in the hover tooltip. Filled bubble with a white letter, dashed connector back to the exit price: S = stop (SL1 / BE / trail / SL2), T2 = TP2, F = HTF CBC flip against the trade, E = 17:00 end of day, R = replaced by a new setup (exit at that close); T1 = TP1 partial (not an exit). Green = profit, red = loss.")
ats_ex_tiny = input.bool(true, "  ↳ exit markers as lettered bubbles off the candles (OFF = text labels)", inline="ats_ext", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.68: the '80% @ TP1' and SL exit markers become a small hollow circled letter at the exit price -- green Ⓣ = TP1 partial, Ⓢ = stop exit (green = runner closed in profit, red = loss / breakeven) -- with the full text in the hover tooltip. v9.69: placed past the candle on their own side (Ⓣ beyond TP, Ⓢ beyond SL) with a dotted connector to the exit price. OFF = text labels at the price.")
ats_ex_tr = input.int(25, "label transp. %", minval=0, maxval=100, step=5, inline="ats_ext", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.70: background transparency of the TP1 / SL exit text labels (used when the symbols box is OFF). 0 = solid, 100 = invisible.")
ats_done_op = input.int(10, "Finished setup fill opacity (%)", minval=0, maxval=100, step=5, group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.28: once a setup has ended, its boxes keep their outline and labels and the green / red fill fades to this opacity (0 = no fill, 100 = solid). The live setup keeps the normal Reward / Risk zone colours.")
ats_cap_on = input.bool(true, "Max ATR SL1 (pts) per symbol", inline="ats_cap", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.07: SL method 3m ATR only. When SL1 = Entry -/+ SL1 x ATR would be farther than the listed points from Entry, SL1 is placed at exactly that distance instead (Trade Levels / alert then show the smaller multiplier, e.g. 1.2×ATR). Format: SYMBOL points, comma separated (MGC 12, MES 8 ...). Full-size contracts use the micro's value (GC = MGC, ES = MES, NQ = MNQ, RTY = M2K, CL = MCL); BTC = MBT or any BTC symbol. Not listed or 0 = no cap. Minimum SL distance still wins if it is larger.")
ats_cap_txt = input.string("MGC 7, MES 8, MNQ 30, M2K 5, MCL 0.3, BTC 500", "", inline="ats_cap", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_tpc_on = input.bool(true, "Max ATR TP1 (pts) per symbol", inline="ats_tpc", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.92: TP method 3m ATR only. When TP1 x ATR is farther than this many points from Entry, TP1 is placed at the cap and the multiplier shown drops (e.g. 1.0×ATR (6.1) for MGC 6). Unlisted symbol = no cap. TP2 is not capped.")
ats_tpc_txt = input.string("MGC 6, MES 6, MNQ 40, M2K 3, MCL 0.3, BTC 300", "", inline="ats_tpc", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
float ats_atr = ta.atr(ats_atr_len)
var float[] ats_alt = array.new_float(13, na)
ats_info_on = input.bool(true, "Show ⓘ setup info label (hover: trigger, CBC 3m/15m)", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v8.92: a small ⓘ just left of each new setup's Entry. Hover it to see LONG/SHORT, the trigger(s) that drew it, CBC direction on the chart TF and HTF, flip side (TOWARD/AWAY), flip flop and Fib zone.")
mk_n = input.int(200, "Keep only the last N chart markers (0 = all)", minval=0, maxval=500, group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.79: TradingView keeps only the newest 500 labels per indicator; the oldest are deleted first, which is why older setups lose their ⓘ and Ⓣ/Ⓢ exit marks. This caps the marker labels (3m CBC flip triangles, reversal triangles, ORB X, HTF flip dots, HTF LONG/SHORT labels, alert dots and letters) at the newest N, so the setup ⓘ and exit marks survive further back. 0 = no cap (old behavior).")
ats_hc_on = input.bool(true, "Setups: act on HTF flip at the HTF candle close", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v8.94: OFF = the setup engine uses the confirmed HTF CBC, which on past candles registers about one HTF candle late (e.g. the 8:30-8:45 flip shows at ~8:57). ON (default since v9.00) = on the last chart candle of each HTF candle (e.g. 8:42-8:45 on 3m/15m) the setup engine reads the HTF CBC as it closes, so the old setup ends and the HTF CBC Flip setup draws at 8:45 -- same on history and live. Only the setup engine (triggers, cooldown exception, setup end, ⓘ label); flip labels, dots and alerts are unchanged.")
ats_cv_on = input.bool(false, "Setups use closed 15m values only (no look-ahead)", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v10.35: OFF (default) = the HTF EMA9 / EMA20 Pierce triggers and the HTF EMA slope / flip-distance checks read the 15m EMA of the candle still forming. Live that is the value so far; when the chart redraws history it is the final value of that 15m candle, so history can show setups the live alert never fired (or on another candle). ON = on every 3m candle except the one that closes the 15m candle, they use the last CLOSED 15m EMA (on the closing candle, that 15m candle's final value) -- the same number live and on history, so the chart's setups match the alerts. Live, the EMA used can be up to one 15m candle old. Test on one chart first.")
ats_cd_bars = input.int(10, "Min candles between setups", minval=1, group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v8.85/v8.87: after a setup is drawn, no new setup from any trigger until this many candles have passed (10 = the 10th candle after the setup is the first allowed). Exceptions: HTF CBC Flip setups, and once the HTF CBC has flipped against the last setup, setups in the new direction may draw immediately.")
ats_q_on = input.bool(true, "No new setups between (ET)", inline="ats_q", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v8.81: no new Trade Setup from any trigger on a candle that opens inside this New York time window (default 16:00-18:00, the daily close / reopen). Alerts and setups already on the chart are not affected.")
ats_q_win = input.session("1600-1845", "", inline="ats_q", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_orb_f = input.bool(true, "No new setups during opening range (forming):  NY", inline="ats_orbf", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.58: no new setup from any trigger on a candle inside the ticked session's opening range window (session open + the OR length set in Opening Range (Sessions), default 30 min: NY 9:30-10:00, London 3:00-3:30, Asia 20:00-20:30 ET). Needs that session's ORB on.")
ats_orb_f_ln = input.bool(true, "London", inline="ats_orbf", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_orb_f_as = input.bool(true, "Asia", inline="ats_orbf", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_orb_in = input.bool(false, "No new setups inside opening range (after set):  NY", inline="ats_orbi", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v9.58: once the ticked session's opening range is complete, no new setup while the candle closes between that OR High and OR Low. Applies until that session's next open resets its range.")
ats_orb_in_ln = input.bool(false, "London", inline="ats_orbi", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_orb_in_as = input.bool(false, "Asia", inline="ats_orbi", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_eod_end = input.bool(true, "End setups at 16:00 ET", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v10.10: On (default): the active setup ends on the bar that closes at 16:00 New York time (Setup Ended \"16:00\", exit marker E) and stays on the chart. No new setup is drawn from 16:00 until the 17:00 CME close; the evening session (18:00+) is unchanged."),
ats_lvl_tbl_show = input.bool(true, "Show Trade Levels box", inline="ats_lvltbl", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Small box listing TP2, TP1, Entry, live Price, SL1 and SL2 of the current Auto Trade Setup, with points from price.")
ats_lvl_tbl_pos = input.string("Top right", "", options=["Top left", "Top center", "Top right", "Middle left", "Middle center", "Middle right", "Bottom left", "Bottom center", "Bottom right"], inline="ats_lvltbl", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
ats_rr_tbl_pos = input.string("Middle right", "R:R table position", options=["Top left", "Top center", "Top right", "Middle left", "Middle center", "Middle right", "Bottom left", "Bottom center", "Bottom right"], group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="v8.47: the small reward:risk table (Entry / Now x TP1/SL1, TP2/SL2). Shown with the Trade Levels table. Pick a spot not used by another table.")
ats_lvl_tbl_size = input.string("Small", "", options=["Tiny", "Small", "Normal", "Large", "Huge"], inline="ats_lvltbl", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌① Auto Trade Setup ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")

// v7.98: Pivot Points input group moved here (right after Auto Trade Setup) per direct request.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════
//  PIVOT POINTS (Daily, Standard/Floor formula)
//  PP = (H+L+C)/3, R1 = 2*PP-L, S1 = 2*PP-H, R2 = PP+(H-L), S2 = PP-(H-L),
//  R3 = H+2*(PP-L), S3 = L-2*(H-PP) — computed from the PRIOR completed daily bar.
//  Distinct from the existing "Pivot (LTF/HTF/MTF)" rows, which are swing high/low fractals
//  (ta.pivothigh/pivotlow), not this classic floor-trader formula.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════
show_pivot_points = input.bool(true, "Enable Pivot Points (Daily)", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Computes PP/R1-3/S1-3 from the prior")
pivot_formula = input.string("Standard", "Visual Pivot Type", options=["Standard", "Camarilla", "Woodie", "Fibonacci"], group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Standard/Floor: PP=(H+L+C)/3,")
show_pivot_pp = input.bool(true, "PP", inline="pivshow1", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
show_pivot_r1 = input.bool(true, "R1", inline="pivshow1", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
show_pivot_s1 = input.bool(true, "S1", inline="pivshow1", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
show_pivot_r2 = input.bool(false, "R2", inline="pivshow2", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
show_pivot_s2 = input.bool(false, "S2", inline="pivshow2", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
show_pivot_r3 = input.bool(false, "R3", inline="pivshow3", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
show_pivot_s3 = input.bool(false, "S3", inline="pivshow3", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
// v7.32: per direct request ("add yesterdays high and low for the current session into the pivots") —
// Yesterday's High/Low (YDH/YDL, the same prior-RTH-session values already tracked elsewhere in this
// file for Next Target/Stop Levels) added as two extra rows in the Pivot Points TABLE only. Scoped to
// the table's own local arrays (see f_render_pivot_table() below), NOT added to piv_price_arr/
// piv_enabled/the crossing arrays — those are shared with f_fire_alerts() (already close to Pine's
// 254-external-element ceiling, CE10116) and the pivot touch-dot loop, and this request only asked
// for the table display, not new YDH/YDL crossing alerts or touch dots.
show_pivot_ydh = input.bool(true, "YD High", inline="pivshow4", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Yesterday's prior-session High, shown as an extra row in the Pivot Points table below (same YDH value the Next Target/Stop Levels row and Status table already use).")
show_pivot_ydl = input.bool(true, "YD Low", inline="pivshow4", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Yesterday's prior-session Low, shown as an extra row in the Pivot Points table below (same YDL value the Next Target/Stop Levels row and Status table already use).")
// v7.37: per direct request ("as orb H ln orb h as orb l ny orb l pp pml etc"), made against a
// screenshot circling the chart's own Reference Levels column — added the same treatment to PMH/
// PML and the 3 session Opening Range highs/lows. Each gets its own dedicated table-scoped toggle,
// same "separate from the shared line-visibility inputs" reasoning as show_pivot_ydh/ydl above.
show_pivot_pmh = input.bool(true, "Premarket High", inline="pivshow5", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Premarket high (same PMH value the Next Target/Stop Levels row and on-chart Reference Levels already use), shown as an extra column in the Pivot Points table below.")
show_pivot_pml = input.bool(true, "Premarket Low", inline="pivshow5", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Premarket low (same PML value the Next Target/Stop Levels row and on-chart Reference Levels already use), shown as an extra column in the Pivot Points table below.")
show_pivot_ny_orh = input.bool(true, "NY Opening Range High", inline="pivshow6", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="NY session's Opening Range High, shown as an extra column in the Pivot Points table below.")
show_pivot_ny_orl = input.bool(true, "NY Opening Range Low", inline="pivshow6", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="NY session's Opening Range Low, shown as an extra column in the Pivot Points table below.")
show_pivot_ln_orh = input.bool(true, "London Opening Range High", inline="pivshow7", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="London session's Opening Range High, shown as an extra column in the Pivot Points table below.")
show_pivot_ln_orl = input.bool(true, "London Opening Range Low", inline="pivshow7", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="London session's Opening Range Low, shown as an extra column in the Pivot Points table below.")
show_pivot_as_orh = input.bool(true, "Asia Opening Range High", inline="pivshow8", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Asia session's Opening Range High, shown as an extra column in the Pivot Points table below.")
show_pivot_as_orl = input.bool(true, "Asia Opening Range Low", inline="pivshow8", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Asia session's Opening Range Low, shown as an extra column in the Pivot Points table below.")
// v7.39: per direct request ("include bsrg if within 4 bars htf and htf pivots as seen in image").
// BRSG-H/BRSG-L share one toggle (the pair is one zone, not two independent levels) and are
// additionally gated by htf_bars_since_flip <= 4 at the call site below — the same recency window
// this file already uses for the HTF Flip confluence factor (v7.31). HTF Piv-H/HTF Piv-L get their
// own separate toggles, no recency gating (matches every other pool addition in this table).
show_pivot_brsg = input.bool(true, "BRSG Zone", inline="pivshow9", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="BRSG Zone's own High/Low price edges, shown as extra columns in the Pivot Points table below — only while within 4 HTF bars of the last HTF CBC flip (same recency window the HTF Flip confluence factor uses).")
show_pivot_htf_piv_hi = input.bool(true, "HTF Pivot High", inline="pivshow10", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Most recent HTF swing pivot high (same value the Status table's \"Pivot (HTF)\" row already uses), shown as an extra column in the Pivot Points table below.")
show_pivot_htf_piv_lo = input.bool(true, "HTF Pivot Low", inline="pivshow10", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Most recent HTF swing pivot low (same value the Status table's \"Pivot (HTF)\" row already uses), shown as an extra column in the Pivot Points table below.")
// v7.40: per direct request ("can the pine script identify equal highs and lows from htf to
// include i table of pivots"). New HTF Equal Highs/Lows detection (separate from the existing LTF-
// only EQH/EQL feature above) — see htf_eqh_price/htf_eql_price near the HTF pivot/structure block
// for the actual detection logic. Sticky until a new HTF EQH/EQL fires, same as every other pool
// entry — na (and therefore hidden) until the first one is detected.
show_pivot_htf_eqh = input.bool(true, "HTF Equal High (EQH)", inline="pivshow11", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Most recent HTF Equal High — two consecutive HTF pivot highs within the same ATR-scaled tolerance the LTF Equal Highs/Lows feature uses, computed on HTF bars. Shown as an extra column in the Pivot Points table below once one is detected.")
show_pivot_htf_eql = input.bool(true, "HTF Equal Low (EQL)", inline="pivshow11", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Most recent HTF Equal Low — two consecutive HTF pivot lows within the same ATR-scaled tolerance the LTF Equal Highs/Lows feature uses, computed on HTF bars. Shown as an extra column in the Pivot Points table below once one is detected.")
// v7.41: per direct follow-up ("show all pivots in table"), scoped via AskUserQuestion to option 1:
// dedicated TABLE-ONLY always-on toggles for R2/R3/S2/S3, independent of both their existing chart-
// line toggle (show_pivot_r2/r3/s2/s3, which stays off by default so the chart itself is unchanged)
// and the v7.38 price-based auto-escalation (which still applies on top of this — whichever is true
// wins). Default true, so R2/R3/S2/S3 now show in the table unconditionally out of the box.
show_pivot_tbl_r2 = input.bool(true, "R2 (table only)", inline="pivshow12", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Always show R2 in the Pivot Points table below, independent of R2's own chart-line toggle above and the price-based auto-escalation.")
show_pivot_tbl_r3 = input.bool(true, "R3 (table only)", inline="pivshow12", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Always show R3 in the Pivot Points table below, independent of R3's own chart-line toggle above and the price-based auto-escalation.")
show_pivot_tbl_s2 = input.bool(true, "S2 (table only)", inline="pivshow13", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Always show S2 in the Pivot Points table below, independent of S2's own chart-line toggle above and the price-based auto-escalation.")
show_pivot_tbl_s3 = input.bool(true, "S3 (table only)", inline="pivshow13", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Always show S3 in the Pivot Points table below, independent of S3's own chart-line toggle above and the price-based auto-escalation.")
// v7.41: per the same follow-up ("also include LTF pivots (see image) and ema200 and vwap") — LTF
// swing pivot High/Low (l_last_hi/l_last_lo, the same values the Structure HH/HL/LH/LL classifier
// and f_render_status_table()'s "Pivot (LTF)" row already use), EMA 200 (ema200), and VWAP
// (vwap_value) added as 6 more always-shown candidates, same reuse-existing-values pattern as every
// prior pool addition. Each gets its own dedicated table-scoped toggle, default true.
show_pivot_ltf_piv_hi = input.bool(true, "LTF Pivot High", inline="pivshow14", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Most recent LTF swing pivot high (same value the Status table's \"Pivot (LTF)\" row already uses), shown as an extra column in the Pivot Points table below.")
show_pivot_ltf_piv_lo = input.bool(true, "LTF Pivot Low", inline="pivshow14", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Most recent LTF swing pivot low (same value the Status table's \"Pivot (LTF)\" row already uses), shown as an extra column in the Pivot Points table below.")
show_pivot_ema200 = input.bool(true, "EMA 200", inline="pivshow15", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="The chart-timeframe 200 EMA, shown as an extra column in the Pivot Points table below.")
show_pivot_vwap = input.bool(true, "VWAP", inline="pivshow15", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Session VWAP, shown as an extra column in the Pivot Points table below.")
show_pivot_table = input.bool(false, "Show Pivot Points table on chart", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="A small dedicated table (separate from")
// v7.36: "Show only closest N" toggle removed — as of v7.36 the table always shows the full fixed
// 9-slot pool (R3/R2/R1/PP/S1/S2/S3 + YD-H/YD-L = 4 above PP, PP, 4 below PP when all enabled),
// so a closest-N distance filter no longer applies. **v7.37: the pool is no longer fixed at 9** —
// PMH/PML and the 3 sessions' Opening Range H/L were added as 8 more always-shown candidates (see
// their own inputs above), so PP is no longer guaranteed to land in the exact middle column once
// any of those are enabled. Individual pivot types are still toggleable via their existing R/S/PP
// show inputs, show_pivot_ydh/show_pivot_ydl, and the 8 new v7.37 toggles above.
pivot_table_position = input.string("Bottom left", "Table position", options=["Top left", "Top center", "Top right", "Middle left", "Middle center", "Middle right", "Bottom left", "Bottom center", "Bottom right"], group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
pivot_table_near_n = input.int(8, "Levels shown each side of price", minval=0, group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="The table only shows this many levels on each side of the Price column (the ones closest to price), so it fits on the chart. 0 = show every level.")
// v7.41: default shrunk to "Tiny" per direct request ("reduce text size to shrink lateral
// distance") — the table has grown to up to 27 columns as of this round, so a smaller default
// font keeps its total on-chart width more manageable.
// v7.42: default bumped back up one size to "Small" per direct follow-up ("one size larger text"),
// now that the table has been seen live at "Tiny". Anyone who already saved their own choice keeps
// it; this only changes what a fresh install/reset sees.
pivot_table_text_size = input.string("Normal", "Table text size", options=["Tiny", "Small", "Normal", "Large", "Huge"], group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
alert_on_pivot_cross = input.bool(true, "Key Level Alert (PP/R1/R2/R3/S1/S2/S3)", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌⑤ Alerts ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Fires once per enabled pivot level.")
show_pivot_lines = input.bool(true, "Draw Pivot Point lines on chart", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Horizontal lines for whichever of")
col_piv_r = input.color(#ff0000, "Resistance (R1/R2/R3)", inline="pivcol", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
col_piv_pp = input.color(#000000, "PP", inline="pivcol", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
col_piv_s = input.color(#22c55e, "Support (S1/S2/S3)", inline="pivcol", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
piv_line_width = input.int(1, "Pivot line width", minval=1, group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
// v6.87: pivot-level touch markers, per direct request/discussion ("add a plain touch - can you add
// tool tips for touches?"). Unlike Key Level Alert (which only fires on a CLOSE crossing a level,
// ta.crossover(close, ...)), this fires on a plain bar-range TOUCH (low <= level and high >= level) —
// closer to the existing VWAP/EMA200/EMA20/HTF EMA9/HTF EMA20 touch dots than to Key Level Alert.
// Built as small labels (not plot() circles) specifically so each one can carry a tooltip naming the
// exact level + price — plot() cannot carry tooltips at all, and a plain colored dot alone would be
// ambiguous with 7 levels potentially close together (unlike VWAP/EMA200, each on its own single
// line). Edge-triggered (fires once at the first bar of each touch streak, not every bar price sits
// on the level) so it doesn't spend the label budget every bar during a multi-bar hover. One shared
// color across all 7 levels, per the agreed scope — existing 5 touch dots intentionally left as
// plain plot() dots, no tooltip retrofit.
show_pivot_touch_dots = input.bool(true, "Touch dots (PP/R1-3/S1-3)", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Marks every bar whose range touches any enabled pivot level — a plain range touch, independent of Key Level Alert's close-confirmed cross. v6.93: rebuilt as a plot() circle (smaller than the old label version); no per-touch tooltip naming the level/price anymore, since plot() can't carry one.")
col_pivot_touch = input.color(color.silver, "Touch dot color", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌④ Pivot Points ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")

show_reversal = input.bool(true, "Show CBC Reversal", inline="reversal", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌⑥ LTF Signals ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Highlight consecutive CBC flips as CBC")
cbc_flip_triangle_size = input.string("Tiny", "CBC Flip Triangle Size", options=["Tiny", "Small", "Normal", "Large", "Huge"], group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌⑥ LTF Signals ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━")
show_ema_touch_dots = input.bool(true, "EMA20 touch dots", inline="ema20t", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌⑥ LTF Signals ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip=tt_touch_dots)
show_vwap_touch_dots = input.bool(true, "VWAP touch dots", inline="vwapt", group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌⑥ LTF Signals ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip=tt_touch_dots)
