// v7.02: mirrors the HTF CBC Flip dot's "which to draw" mode (see htf_flip_dot_mode under Alerts),
// per direct request ("can we have an input switch which tells only to use anticipatory in drawing
// dots vs anticipatory and closed"), extended to the arrows too per follow-up scoping confirmation.
// Arrows previously had NO anticipatory option at all — always confirmed-only, same lag as the dot
// had before v6.52. Default "Confirmed Only" preserves that exact pre-v7.02 behavior for anyone who
// already has arrows on; switching to "Anticipatory Only" or "Both" opts into the new early-fire
// behavior (see htf_flip_arrow_early_bull/bear below, which mirrors the dot's own
// htf_flip_early_marker_bull/bear mechanism — same seconds-before-close gate, own separate de-dup
// latch).
htf_flip_arrow_mode = input.string("Anticipatory Only", "HTF Flip Arrows: which to draw", options=["Confirmed Only", "Anticipatory Only", "Both"], group="▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌▌⑪ HTF Signals ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━", tooltip="Confirmed Only: the arrow appears only once the HTF bar has fully closed and confirmed its direction — the original pre-v7.02 lag. Anticipatory Only (default as of v7.03): only the early arrow appears — once the HTF bar is within N seconds of its scheduled close (same seconds input the HTF CBC Flip dot uses, under Alerts) if the live/still-forming direction already differs from the last confirmed direction — the regular confirmed arrow never appears afterward, even once that HTF bar actually closes. Both: shows both — an early arrow, then the regular confirmed arrow once the HTF bar actually closes, even when they end up agreeing. The early arrow can very rarely be followed by an OPPOSITE-direction arrow (when switched to \"Both\") if price reverses in that last sliver before the HTF bar actually closes — same repaint tradeoff as the dot's own anticipatory mode. Has no effect if HTF Flip Arrows above is off.")
// v7.05: htf_flip_arrow_show_confirmed removed as a separate named var (it was read at exactly ONE
// real call site, the confirmed arrow's drawing "if" below) -- inlined there directly.
// htf_flip_arrow_show_anticipatory stays as a named var since it's read at 2 real call sites
// (htf_flip_arrow_early_bull/bear).
htf_flip_arrow_show_anticipatory = htf_flip_arrow_mode != "Confirmed Only"
