// v6.39 token-trim: "show_level_name or show_level_price" appeared byte-for-byte 16 times, always at
// top level (never crossing into a user-defined function — the specific thing that backfired for
// f_market_session_et/f_fmt_ny_time per this file's own history) — a real common-subexpression, not a
// literal-string dedup (which v4.24/v4.25 already confirmed saves nothing). Hoisted to one shared
// top-level bool, referenced at all 16 sites instead of re-evaluating the "or" each time.
